{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:40:35.346389", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_taken = []\n  \n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Define action IDs for better readability and direct use\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = (action_map['UP'], action_map['DOWN'],\n                                action_map['LEFT'], action_map['RIGHT'],\n                                action_map['USE'])\n  \n  # Mapping of (dx, dy) coordinate changes to their corresponding action IDs.\n  # This facilitates movement calculations within the BFS.\n  # CraftWorld agent position `pos` is (column, row) or (x, y).\n  # UP: decreases row (y), DOWN: increases row (y)\n  # LEFT: decreases column (x), RIGHT: increases column (x)\n  move_deltas_to_action = {\n      (0, -1): UP,    # Change in (x, y) for UP action\n      (0, 1): DOWN,   # Change in (x, y) for DOWN action\n      (-1, 0): LEFT,  # Change in (x, y) for LEFT action\n      (1, 0): RIGHT   # Change in (x, y) for RIGHT action\n  }\n  \n  world = env.world # Reference to the CraftWorld instance for environment details\n  \n  # Primitives are items that can be picked up. If the target `primitive`\n  # is not in the list of grabbable items, this function cannot collect it.\n  if primitive not in world.grabbable_indices:\n      # Return an empty list of actions, as the item is uncollectible by this method.\n      return []\n\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 200 # A safety limit to prevent infinite loops in complex or unreachable scenarios.\n\n  def find_path_bfs(start_pos, target_kind_idx, current_grid, world_ref):\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from `start_pos`\n      to any cell that contains `target_kind_idx`.\n      \n      Args:\n          start_pos (tuple): The agent's current (x, y) grid coordinates.\n          target_kind_idx (int): The integer index of the item kind to find.\n          current_grid (numpy.ndarray): The current grid layout (WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS).\n          world_ref (CraftWorld): Reference to the CraftWorld instance, used to determine obstacles.\n\n      Returns:\n          list: A list of action IDs representing the shortest sequence of moves to reach\n                a cell containing the target kind. Returns None if no path is found.\n      \"\"\"\n      grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_grid.shape\n\n      # Identify grid entities that act as obstacles and cannot be traversed.\n      # This typically includes non-grabbable environment items (e.g., water, stone)\n      # and static workshop locations (e.g., workbench, furnace).\n      obstacle_indices = world_ref.non_grabbable_indices.union(world_ref.workshop_indices)\n\n      def is_walkable(x, y):\n          \"\"\"Checks if a given grid cell (x, y) is within bounds and free of obstacles.\"\"\"\n          if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n              return False # Coordinates are out of the grid boundaries\n          \n          # Iterate through known obstacle kinds to check if the cell is blocked.\n          # Grabbable items (like the primitive itself) are usually traversable.\n          for idx in obstacle_indices:\n              if current_grid[x, y, idx] == 1:\n                  return False # The cell contains an impassable obstacle\n          return True # The cell is within bounds and can be walked upon\n\n      # Initialize BFS queue with the starting position and an empty path.\n      queue = deque([(start_pos, [])])\n      # Keep track of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant work.\n      visited = {start_pos}\n\n      while queue:\n          (curr_x, curr_y), path = queue.popleft()\n\n          # Check if the current cell in the BFS path contains the target item.\n          # If so, this path leads directly to the item.\n          if current_grid[curr_x, curr_y, target_kind_idx] == 1:\n              return path # Return the sequence of movement actions to reach this cell.\n\n          # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n          for (dx, dy), action_id in move_deltas_to_action.items():\n              next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n              next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n              # If the neighbor is walkable and has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n              if is_walkable(next_x, next_y) and next_pos not in visited:\n                  visited.add(next_pos)\n                  queue.append((next_pos, path + [action_id]))\n      \n      return None # No path found to any instance of the primitive on the grid.\n\n  # Main loop for the collection process, executing actions step-by-step.\n  for _ in range(MAX_COLLECT_STEPS):\n      # Access the current state of the environment for real-time decision making.\n      current_state = env._current_state \n      \n      # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory.\n      # This is the primary success condition and exit point.\n      if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n          return actions_taken # Goal achieved: primitive has been collected.\n\n      current_pos = current_state.pos # Agent's current (x, y) grid position.\n      grid = current_state.grid       # The current environmental grid layout.\n      \n      # 2. Check if the primitive is within the agent's 3x3 neighborhood (including its own cell).\n      # If so, the agent can attempt to pick it up using the 'USE' action.\n      # The `next_to` method conveniently checks this proximity.\n      if current_state.next_to(primitive):\n          # Perform the 'USE' action. This should pick up the primitive if successful.\n          _reward, done, _observations = env.step(USE) \n          actions_taken.append(USE)\n          if done:\n              # If the environment signals the episode is finished (e.g., max_steps reached),\n              # break the collection loop.\n              break \n          continue # After using, immediately re-check inventory in the next iteration.\n\n      # 3. If the primitive is not in inventory and not adjacent, find the shortest path\n      # to any instance of the primitive on the grid using BFS.\n      path_to_primitive = find_path_bfs(current_pos, primitive, grid, world)\n\n      if path_to_primitive:\n          # If a path is found, take the very first step on that calculated path.\n          # This moves the agent one step closer to the primitive.\n          next_action = path_to_primitive[0]\n          _reward, done, _observations = env.step(next_action) \n          actions_taken.append(next_action)\n          if done:\n              # If the episode ends after this movement, break the loop.\n              break\n      else:\n          # If no path could be found to any primitive on the grid, it means\n          # the primitive might be unreachable, or all instances have been collected,\n          # or it disappeared. In this case, further collection attempts are futile.\n          break \n\n  return actions_taken # Return the sequence of actions taken during the collection attempt.", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:40:36.323209", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  from collections import deque\n\n  actions_taken = []\n  \n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Unpack action IDs for clarity and direct use\n  UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = (action_map['UP'], action_map['DOWN'],\n                                action_map['LEFT'], action_map['RIGHT'],\n                                action_map['USE'])\n  \n  # Helper for action to delta mapping (for BFS pathfinding)\n  # Assumes UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT are absolute movements, not relative turns.\n  MOVE_ACTIONS_DELTAS = {\n      UP: (0, -1),\n      DOWN: (0, 1),\n      LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT: (1, 0)\n  }\n  \n  # Helper for cardinal directions and their corresponding integer IDs\n  # Assuming CraftState.dir maps as: 0: UP, 1: RIGHT, 2: DOWN, 3: LEFT\n  DIR_TO_OFFSET = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # UP (North)\n      1: (1, 0),   # RIGHT (East)\n      2: (0, 1),   # DOWN (South)\n      3: (-1, 0)   # LEFT (West)\n  }\n  OFFSET_TO_DIR = {\n      (0, -1): 0,\n      (1, 0): 1,\n      (0, 1): 2,\n      (-1, 0): 3\n  }\n  \n  world = env.world # Get reference to the CraftWorld instance for environment details\n  \n  # Primitives are items that can be picked up. If the goal `primitive` is not\n  # in the list of grabbable items, this function cannot collect it.\n  if primitive not in world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 200 # A safety limit to prevent infinite loops\n\n  # Define what entity types act as obstacles (cannot be walked through).\n  # This typically includes non-grabbable environment items (like water, stone)\n  # and workshop locations (like workbench, furnace).\n  obstacle_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices.union(world.workshop_indices)\n\n  def _is_valid_pos(x, y, grid_shape, current_grid):\n      \"\"\"Checks if a given grid cell (x, y) is within bounds and contains no obstacles.\"\"\"\n      width, height, _ = grid_shape\n      if not (0 <= x < width and 0 <= y < height):\n          return False # Out of bounds\n      # Check if the cell contains any obstacle kind\n      for idx in obstacle_indices:\n          if current_grid[x, y, idx] == 1:\n              return False # Contains an obstacle\n      return True # The cell is within bounds and free of obstacles\n\n  def _turns_to_align(current_dir, target_dir):\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the number of left and right turns to align current_dir with target_dir.\n      Returns (num_left_turns, num_right_turns).\n      \"\"\"\n      # Calculate difference in direction indices (0-3)\n      delta = (target_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n      \n      if delta == 0:\n          return 0, 0  # Already aligned\n      elif delta == 1:\n          return 0, 1  # 1 Right turn (0 Left turns)\n      elif delta == 2:\n          return 2, 2  # 2 Left or 2 Right turns (arbitrarily provide both)\n      elif delta == 3:\n          return 1, 0  # 1 Left turn (0 Right turns)\n\n  def find_path_bfs(start_pos, target_primitive_idx, current_grid):\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path from `start_pos`\n      to any *adjacent* walkable cell from which `target_primitive_idx` can be `USE`d.\n      \n      Args:\n          start_pos (tuple): Agent's current (x, y) position.\n          target_primitive_idx (int): The index of the primitive kind to find.\n          current_grid (numpy.ndarray): The current state of the grid.\n          \n      Returns:\n          list: A list of action IDs representing the shortest path, or None if no path found.\n      \"\"\"\n      grid_width, grid_height, _ = current_grid.shape\n\n      queue = deque([(start_pos, [])])\n      visited = {start_pos}\n\n      while queue:\n          (curr_x, curr_y), path = queue.popleft()\n\n          # Check if (curr_x, curr_y) is a valid position from which to USE the primitive\n          # This means checking its four cardinal neighbors.\n          for dx_check, dy_check in DIR_TO_OFFSET.values(): # Iterate over cardinal offsets\n              adj_x, adj_y = curr_x + dx_check, curr_y + dy_check\n              \n              # Check if this adjacent cell is within bounds and contains the primitive\n              if (0 <= adj_x < grid_width and 0 <= adj_y < grid_height) and \\\n                 current_grid[adj_x, adj_y, target_primitive_idx] == 1:\n                  # Found a primitive cardinally adjacent to (curr_x, curr_y).\n                  # This means (curr_x, curr_y) is a suitable target cell for the agent.\n                  return path # Return the path to this suitable cell\n\n          # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n          for action_val, (dx, dy) in MOVE_ACTIONS_DELTAS.items():\n              next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n              next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n              # Use the outer `_is_valid_pos` helper, passing necessary context.\n              if _is_valid_pos(next_x, next_y, current_grid.shape, current_grid) and next_pos not in visited:\n                  visited.add(next_pos)\n                  queue.append((next_x, next_y, path + [action_val]))\n\n      return None # No path found\n\n  # Main loop for the collection process\n  for _ in range(MAX_COLLECT_STEPS):\n      # Access the current state of the environment\n      current_state = env._current_state\n      current_pos = current_state.pos\n      current_dir = current_state.dir\n      grid = current_state.grid\n      grid_shape = grid.shape\n\n      # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory\n      if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n          return actions_taken # Goal achieved, primitive collected\n\n      # 2. Check if the primitive is directly in front of the agent and can be USEd.\n      # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      front_x, front_y = current_pos[0] + DIR_TO_OFFSET[current_dir][0], \\\n                         current_pos[1] + DIR_TO_OFFSET[current_dir][1]\n\n      # Check if the cell in front is valid and contains the primitive.\n      if _is_valid_pos(front_x, front_y, grid_shape, grid) and grid[front_x, front_y, primitive] == 1:\n          # Primitive is directly in front, so USE it.\n          _reward, done, _observations = env.step(USE)\n          actions_taken.append(USE)\n          if done:\n              break # Episode ended (e.g., max_steps reached)\n          continue # Re-check inventory in the next iteration after using\n\n      # 3. If not directly in front, check if the primitive is in the cardinal neighborhood\n      # but the agent is facing the wrong way.\n      target_dir_to_face = None\n      # Iterate over cardinal neighbor offsets to find the primitive\n      for offset_dx, offset_dy in DIR_TO_OFFSET.values():\n          neighbor_x, neighbor_y = current_pos[0] + offset_dx, current_pos[1] + offset_dy\n          if _is_valid_pos(neighbor_x, neighbor_y, grid_shape, grid) and \\\n             grid[neighbor_x, neighbor_y, primitive] == 1:\n              # Found a primitive in a cardinal neighbor cell.\n              # Determine the direction the agent needs to face to interact with it.\n              target_dir_to_face = OFFSET_TO_DIR[(offset_dx, offset_dy)]\n              break # Found the closest one, no need to check other neighbors\n\n      if target_dir_to_face is not None:\n          # Primitive is adjacent but agent is not facing it.\n          # Calculate and perform turns to face it.\n          num_left, num_right = _turns_to_align(current_dir, target_dir_to_face)\n          \n          if num_left < num_right: # Prioritize left turns if fewer\n              for _ in range(num_left):\n                  _reward, done, _observations = env.step(LEFT)\n                  actions_taken.append(LEFT)\n                  if done: break\n          else: # Otherwise (num_right <= num_left), prioritize right turns\n              for _ in range(num_right):\n                  _reward, done, _observations = env.step(RIGHT)\n                  actions_taken.append(RIGHT)\n                  if done: break\n          \n          if done: break # If an intermediate turn ended the episode\n          continue # After turning, re-evaluate (will hit step 2 in next iteration)\n\n      # 4. If primitive is not in inventory, not directly in front, and not merely misaligned in neighborhood,\n      # then pathfind and move towards it.\n      path_to_adjacent_primitive = find_path_bfs(current_pos, primitive, grid)\n\n      if path_to_adjacent_primitive:\n          # If a path is found, take the first step on that path.\n          next_action = path_to_adjacent_primitive[0]\n          _reward, done, _observations = env.step(next_action) # Perform the movement action\n          actions_taken.append(next_action)\n          if done:\n              break # Episode ended\n      else:\n          # No path found to any instance of the primitive (adjacent to a walkable spot),\n          # or all instances have been collected/are gone/unreachable.\n          break # Cannot collect the primitive, terminate\n\n  return actions_taken", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:42:09.748425", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:42:09.817419", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    current_state = env._current_state\n    \n    # Check if primitive is already in inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    grid = current_state.grid\n    start_pos = current_state.pos\n    initial_dir = current_state.dir\n    \n    WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape # N_KINDS is not needed for movement logic\n\n    # Define action constants based on CraftLab.action_specs\n    # DOWN->0, UP->1, LEFT->2, RIGHT->3, USE->4\n    DOWN = 0\n    UP = 1\n    LEFT = 2\n    RIGHT = 3\n    USE = 4\n\n    # Direction vector mapping: index -> (dx, dy)\n    # This determines what position is \"in front\" of the agent for a given direction.\n    # 0: North (agent facing UP)\n    # 1: East (agent facing RIGHT)\n    # 2: South (agent facing DOWN)\n    # 3: West (agent facing LEFT)\n    DIR_VECS = {\n        0: (0, -1),  # North (dx=0, dy=-1)\n        1: (1, 0),   # East (dx=1, dy=0)\n        2: (0, 1),   # South (dx=0, dy=1)\n        3: (-1, 0)   # West (dx=-1, dy=0)\n    }\n\n    # Mapping of (dx, dy) movement relative to current position to\n    # (action_to_take, resulting_agent_direction_index)\n    # This tells us which action leads to which new position and what direction the agent will be facing.\n    MOVE_ACTIONS_MAP = {\n        (0, -1): (UP, 0),    # Move North (UP), agent faces North (dir 0)\n        (0, 1): (DOWN, 2),   # Move South (DOWN), agent faces South (dir 2)\n        (1, 0): (RIGHT, 1),  # Move East (RIGHT), agent faces East (dir 1)\n        (-1, 0): (LEFT, 3)   # Move West (LEFT), agent faces West (dir 3)\n    }\n\n    # Find all locations of the primitive on the grid\n    target_locations = []\n    for x in range(WIDTH):\n        for y in range(HEIGHT):\n            if grid[x, y, primitive] == 1:\n                target_locations.append((x, y))\n    \n    if not target_locations:\n        return [] # Primitive not found on the grid\n\n    # BFS implementation\n    # Queue stores: (current_position (tuple), list_of_actions_so_far, current_direction (int))\n    q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [], initial_dir)])\n    \n    # Visited set stores ((x, y), direction) tuples to avoid cycles and redundant paths.\n    # We must track direction because the actions and valid 'USE' depend on it.\n    visited = { (start_pos, initial_dir) }\n\n    while q:\n        (cx, cy), current_actions, current_dir = q.popleft()\n\n        # Check if the current position (cx, cy) allows for immediate collection (USE action)\n        # This means (cx,cy) must be adjacent to a target_location AND facing that target.\n        for tx, ty in target_locations:\n            # Calculate the vector from agent's current position to the target\n            vec_to_target_dx, vec_to_target_dy = tx - cx, ty - cy\n            \n            # Check if adjacent (Manhattan distance 1)\n            if abs(vec_to_target_dx) + abs(vec_to_target_dy) == 1:\n                # Determine the direction the agent needs to face to hit this target\n                required_facing_dir = -1\n                for d_idx, (vx, vy) in DIR_VECS.items():\n                    if vx == vec_to_target_dx and vy == vec_to_target_dy:\n                        required_facing_dir = d_idx\n                        break\n                \n                # If the agent is currently facing the required direction, we can use it!\n                if current_dir == required_facing_dir:\n                    return current_actions + [USE]\n\n        # Explore possible movement actions from the current state\n        for (move_dx, move_dy), (action, new_dir) in MOVE_ACTIONS_MAP.items():\n            nx, ny = cx + move_dx, cy + move_dy\n\n            # Check for valid grid boundaries\n            if not (0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT):\n                continue\n            \n            # Check if the new cell (nx,ny) is traversable.\n            # A common assumption is that agents cannot step on the item they are trying to collect,\n            # or other solid obstacles. For `collect_v2`, we assume the primitive itself\n            # is typically not a traversable square if it's an object to be picked up\n            # (e.g., a tree, a rock node).\n            # If the cell (nx, ny) contains the primitive, we avoid stepping on it.\n            if grid[nx, ny, primitive] == 1:\n                continue\n            \n            # Note: A more sophisticated solution might check `env.world.non_grabbable_indices`\n            # for other types of impassable terrain (like walls or deep water without a boat).\n            # For this `v2` version, we stick to boundary checks and avoiding the target primitive itself.\n\n            # Avoid previously visited states (combination of position and direction)\n            if ((nx, ny), new_dir) not in visited:\n                visited.add(((nx, ny), new_dir))\n                q.append(((nx, ny), current_actions + [action], new_dir))\n    \n    return [] # No path found to collect the primitive", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:43:29.409668", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    obs = env.observations()\n    grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n    pos = obs['features_dict']['pos']  # (row, col)\n\n    grid_height, grid_width, num_kinds = grid.shape\n\n    # Get action mappings dynamically from the environment\n    action_map = env.action_specs()\n    DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n    UP = action_map['UP']\n    LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n    RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n    USE = action_map['USE']\n\n    # Define possible movements (dr, dc) and their corresponding actions\n    movements = {\n        (0, 1): RIGHT,  # Move right (increase in column)\n        (0, -1): LEFT,   # Move left (decrease in column)\n        (1, 0): DOWN,   # Move down (increase in row)\n        (-1, 0): UP,    # Move up (decrease in row)\n    }\n\n    # Use collections.deque for efficient BFS queue operations.\n    # Assumes 'collections' module is available in the execution environment\n    # without an explicit import statement inside the function, as per prompt.\n    queue = collections.deque()\n    visited = set()\n\n    # Start BFS from the agent's current position\n    # The queue stores tuples: (current_row, current_col, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n    queue.append((pos[0], pos[1], []))\n    visited.add((pos[0], pos[1]))\n\n    while queue:\n        r, c, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n        # Check if the target primitive is located at the current cell.\n        # A primitive is considered \"present\" if its count at grid[r, c, primitive] is greater than 0.\n        if grid[r, c, primitive] > 0:\n            # If the primitive is found, return the path to reach this cell,\n            # followed by a USE action to collect it.\n            return path_actions + [USE]\n\n        # Explore all valid neighboring cells\n        for (dr, dc), action in movements.items():\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n\n            # Check if the new position (nr, nc) is within the grid boundaries\n            if 0 <= nr < grid_height and 0 <= nc < grid_width:\n                # Check if this cell has already been visited during the BFS\n                # This simple BFS assumes all grid cells within bounds are traversable.\n                # If there were specific impassable terrain types (e.g., walls, water),\n                # an additional check for traversability would be added here\n                # (e.g., `and not grid[nr, nc, WALL_KIND_IDX] > 0`).\n                if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n                    visited.add((nr, nc))\n                    # Add the new position and the updated list of actions to the queue\n                    queue.append((nr, nc, path_actions + [action]))\n\n    # If the BFS completes and the primitive was not found anywhere reachable on the grid,\n    # return an empty list, indicating that it cannot be collected.\n    return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:43:29.480208", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    current_state = env._current_state\n    \n    # Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    grid = current_state.grid\n    grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # grid is (WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS)\n    \n    # Determine if the primitive is grabbable (collected by moving onto it)\n    # or non-grabbable (requires being adjacent and using the USE action).\n    # env.world holds the Cookbook instance which has grabbable/non_grabbable_indices.\n    is_grabbable = primitive in env.world.grabbable_indices\n\n    # BFS setup\n    q = collections.deque()\n    q.append((current_state.pos, [])) # (current_position (tuple), list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n    \n    visited = {current_state.pos} # Set of (x, y) tuples to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n\n    # Action mappings for movement (dx, dy)\n    # DOWN: 0, UP: 1, LEFT: 2, RIGHT: 3, USE: 4\n    # (dx, dy) where dx is change in x (width), dy is change in y (height)\n    move_deltas = {\n        0: (0, 1),   # DOWN (dx=0, dy=1)\n        1: (0, -1),  # UP   (dx=0, dy=-1)\n        2: (-1, 0),  # LEFT (dx=-1, dy=0)\n        3: (1, 0)    # RIGHT (dx=1, dy=0)\n    }\n    move_actions = [0, 1, 2, 3] # List of only movement actions\n    \n    target_path_actions = None\n\n    while q:\n        (cx, cy), c_actions = q.popleft()\n\n        # Check if the current position meets the target criteria for collection\n        if is_grabbable:\n            # If the primitive is grabbable, we just need to reach its location.\n            # It's collected automatically upon entering the square.\n            if grid[cx, cy, primitive] == 1:\n                target_path_actions = c_actions\n                break # Path found, break BFS\n        else:\n            # If the primitive is non-grabbable, the agent needs to be adjacent to it\n            # and then perform a 'USE' action.\n            found_adjacent_primitive = False\n            for dx_adj, dy_adj in move_deltas.values(): # Check all 4 direct neighbors\n                nx_adj, ny_adj = cx + dx_adj, cy + dy_adj\n                \n                # Check bounds and if the primitive is at the adjacent location\n                if (0 <= nx_adj < grid_width and 0 <= ny_adj < grid_height and \n                    grid[nx_adj, ny_adj, primitive] == 1):\n                    \n                    target_path_actions = c_actions + [4] # Add the USE action\n                    found_adjacent_primitive = True\n                    break # Found an adjacent primitive, so this path is a solution\n            \n            if found_adjacent_primitive:\n                break # Path found, break BFS\n\n        # If target not found at current position, explore valid neighboring positions\n        for action in move_actions:\n            dx, dy = move_deltas[action]\n            nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n\n            # Check if the new position is within grid bounds and has not been visited yet\n            if 0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height and (nx, ny) not in visited:\n                visited.add((nx, ny))\n                q.append(((nx, ny), c_actions + [action]))\n\n    # Return the sequence of actions if a path was found, otherwise an empty list\n    return target_path_actions if target_path_actions is not None else []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:44:31.739687", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  from collections import deque\n\n  actions_taken = []\n  \n  # Get action integer IDs from the environment's action_specs\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  \n  # Get references to world for item type information\n  world = env.world\n  \n  # Define a reasonable max number of steps to prevent infinite loops\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 200 \n\n  # Map movement actions to (dx, dy) coordinate changes for BFS\n  # CraftWorld agent position `pos` is (column, row).\n  # UP: decreases row (y), column (x) stays same -> (0, -1)\n  # DOWN: increases row (y), column (x) stays same -> (0, 1)\n  # LEFT: decreases column (x), row (y) stays same -> (-1, 0)\n  # RIGHT: increases column (x), row (y) stays same -> (1, 0)\n  move_deltas = {\n      action_map['UP']: (0, -1),\n      action_map['DOWN']: (0, 1),\n      action_map['LEFT']: (-1, 0),\n      action_map['RIGHT']: (1, 0),\n  }\n  \n  # Helper to check if a position is within grid bounds\n  def _is_valid_pos(x, y, grid_shape):\n      width, height, _ = grid_shape\n      return 0 <= x < width and 0 <= y < height\n\n  # Helper function to find a path to a cell CARDINALLY adjacent to the target primitive\n  # Returns (path_actions, target_primitive_coord) or (None, None)\n  def _find_path_to_cardinal_adjacent(start_pos, target_kind_idx, current_grid, grid_shape):\n      queue = deque([(start_pos[0], start_pos[1], [])]) # (x, y, path_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n      visited = {(start_pos[0], start_pos[1])} # Keep track of visited positions\n      \n      # Cardinal neighbors (dx, dy) relative to agent's potential position for checking if primitive is there\n      cardinal_neighbors_relative = [(0, -1), (1, 0), (0, 1), (-1, 0)] # UP, RIGHT, DOWN, LEFT\n      \n      while queue:\n          px, py, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n          # Check if the current BFS position (px, py) is CARDINALLY adjacent to the primitive\n          target_primitive_location = None\n          for dx_nb, dy_nb in cardinal_neighbors_relative:\n              nx_nb, ny_nb = px + dx_nb, py + dy_nb\n              if _is_valid_pos(nx_nb, ny_nb, grid_shape) and current_grid[nx_nb, ny_nb, target_kind_idx] == 1:\n                  target_primitive_location = (nx_nb, ny_nb)\n                  break\n          \n          if target_primitive_location:\n              # Found a path to a cell (px, py) from which the agent can cardinally interact with the primitive.\n              return path_so_far, target_primitive_location\n              \n          # Explore valid and unvisited neighboring cells for movement\n          for action_val, (dx, dy) in move_deltas.items():\n              next_x, next_y = px + dx, py + dy\n              if _is_valid_pos(next_x, next_y, grid_shape) and (next_x, next_y) not in visited:\n                  visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n                  queue.append((next_x, next_y, path_so_far + [action_val]))\n      \n      return None, None # No path found to a cardinally adjacent cell\n\n  # Check if the primitive is a known grabbable item.\n  if primitive not in world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  current_planned_path = [] # Stores the sequence of movement actions to follow\n  \n  # Main loop for finding and collecting the primitive\n  for _ in range(MAX_COLLECT_STEPS):\n    current_state = env._current_state # Direct access to the internal CraftState\n    \n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return actions_taken # Goal achieved\n\n    # 2. Check if the agent is currently next to the primitive (cardinally), and if so, orient and use it\n    primitive_location_for_use = None\n    agent_x, agent_y = current_state.pos\n    grid = current_state.grid # Use the current grid state for checks\n    \n    # Iterate through cardinal neighborhood to find primitive for direct USE\n    cardinal_neighbors_relative = [(0, -1), (1, 0), (0, 1), (-1, 0)] # UP, RIGHT, DOWN, LEFT\n    for dx_nb, dy_nb in cardinal_neighbors_relative:\n        nx_nb, ny_nb = agent_x + dx_nb, agent_y + dy_nb\n        if _is_valid_pos(nx_nb, ny_nb, grid.shape) and grid[nx_nb, ny_nb, primitive] == 1:\n            primitive_location_for_use = (nx_nb, ny_nb)\n            break\n            \n    if primitive_location_for_use:\n        # Agent is next to a primitive (cardinally). Now orient and USE.\n        target_x, target_y = primitive_location_for_use\n        \n        dx_rel = target_x - agent_x\n        dy_rel = target_y - agent_y\n\n        required_dir = -1\n        # Map (dx, dy) to a direction integer (0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W)\n        # N=0 (0, -1), E=1 (1, 0), S=2 (0, 1), W=3 (-1, 0)\n        if dy_rel == -1 and dx_rel == 0: required_dir = 0 # UP\n        elif dx_rel == 1 and dy_rel == 0: required_dir = 1 # RIGHT\n        elif dy_rel == 1 and dx_rel == 0: required_dir = 2 # DOWN\n        elif dx_rel == -1 and dy_rel == 0: required_dir = 3 # LEFT\n        \n        # This required_dir should always be valid since we found a cardinal neighbor.\n        current_dir = current_state.dir\n        # We must be facing the primitive to USE it. While not facing, turn.\n        while current_dir != required_dir:\n            # Calculate shorter turn (right or left)\n            turn_right_steps = (required_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n            turn_left_steps = (current_dir - required_dir + 4) % 4\n\n            turn_action = action_map['RIGHT'] if turn_right_steps <= turn_left_steps else action_map['LEFT']\n            \n            _reward, done, _observations = env.step(turn_action)\n            actions_taken.append(turn_action)\n            current_state = env._current_state # Update state after turn\n            current_dir = current_state.dir\n            if done:\n                return actions_taken\n\n        # Now agent is oriented, perform USE\n        _reward, done, _observations = env.step(action_map['USE'])\n        actions_taken.append(action_map['USE'])\n        # Clear the current planned path, as the environment might have changed (e.g., item collected).\n        current_planned_path = [] \n        if done:\n            return actions_taken\n        continue # Successfully used, go to next iteration to re-check inventory\n\n    # 3. Path Planning or Path Following\n    if not current_planned_path: # If no path is currently being followed, or it's exhausted\n        # Find a new path to a cell cardinally adjacent to the primitive\n        path_found, _ = _find_path_to_cardinal_adjacent(\n            current_state.pos, \n            primitive, \n            current_state.grid, \n            current_state.grid.shape\n        )\n        \n        if path_found is None:\n            # If no path can be found, primitive is unreachable or doesn't exist.\n            break # Cannot collect\n        else:\n            current_planned_path = path_found # Store the full path to follow\n\n    # 4. Execute the next action in the pre-computed path\n    if current_planned_path:\n        action_to_take = current_planned_path.pop(0) # Take the first step and remove it from the planned path\n        _reward, done, _observations = env.step(action_to_take)\n        actions_taken.append(action_to_take)\n        \n        if done:\n          return actions_taken\n    else:\n        # This branch should ideally not be reached if path_found was not None\n        # and current_planned_path was populated. It acts as a defensive break.\n        break\n            \n  return actions_taken", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:44:32.750555", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  from collections import deque\n\n  actions_taken = []\n  \n  # Get action integer IDs from the environment's action_specs\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  \n  # Get references to world for item type information\n  world = env.world\n  \n  # Define a reasonable max number of steps to prevent infinite loops\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 200 \n\n  # Map movement actions to (dx, dy) coordinate changes for BFS\n  # CraftWorld agent position `pos` is (column, row).\n  # UP: decreases row (y), column (x) stays same -> (0, -1)\n  # DOWN: increases row (y), column (x) stays same -> (0, 1)\n  # LEFT: decreases column (x), row (y) stays same -> (-1, 0)\n  # RIGHT: increases column (x), row (y) stays same -> (1, 0)\n  move_deltas = {\n      action_map['UP']: (0, -1),\n      action_map['DOWN']: (0, 1),\n      action_map['LEFT']: (-1, 0),\n      action_map['RIGHT']: (1, 0),\n  }\n  \n  # Helper to check if a position is within grid bounds\n  def _is_valid_pos(x, y, grid_shape):\n      width, height, _ = grid_shape\n      return 0 <= x < width and 0 <= y < height\n\n  # Check if the primitive is a known grabbable item.\n  # If it's not grabbable, this function cannot collect it.\n  if primitive not in world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # Path to follow, if one has been computed\n  current_path_actions = None\n\n  # Main loop for finding and collecting the primitive\n  for _ in range(MAX_COLLECT_STEPS):\n    current_state = env._current_state # Direct access to the internal CraftState\n    \n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return actions_taken # Goal achieved\n\n    # 2. Check if the agent is currently next to the primitive, and if so, orient and use it\n    primitive_location_nearby = None\n    agent_x, agent_y = current_state.pos\n    grid = current_state.grid # Use the current grid state for checks\n    \n    # Iterate through 3x3 neighborhood (excluding center) to find primitive\n    for dx_nb in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dy_nb in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            if dx_nb == 0 and dy_nb == 0: # Skip agent's own cell (agent is not 'next to' itself)\n                continue\n            \n            nx_nb, ny_nb = agent_x + dx_nb, agent_y + dy_nb\n            if _is_valid_pos(nx_nb, ny_nb, grid.shape) and grid[nx_nb, ny_nb, primitive] == 1:\n                primitive_location_nearby = (nx_nb, ny_nb)\n                break\n        if primitive_location_nearby:\n            break\n            \n    if primitive_location_nearby:\n        # Agent is next to a primitive. Now orient and USE.\n        target_x, target_y = primitive_location_nearby\n        \n        # Calculate required direction from agent_x, agent_y to target_x, target_y\n        dx_rel = target_x - agent_x\n        dy_rel = target_y - agent_y\n\n        required_dir = -1\n        # Map (dx, dy) to a direction integer (0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W) based on CraftWorld conventions\n        # 0: North (UP, dy=-1)\n        # 1: East (RIGHT, dx=1)\n        # 2: South (DOWN, dy=1)\n        # 3: West (LEFT, dx=-1)\n        if dy_rel < 0: # Target is North (UP)\n            required_dir = 0\n        elif dx_rel > 0: # Target is East (RIGHT)\n            required_dir = 1\n        elif dy_rel > 0: # Target is South (DOWN)\n            required_dir = 2\n        elif dx_rel < 0: # Target is West (LEFT)\n            required_dir = 3\n        \n        # Orient the agent if not already facing the required direction\n        current_dir = current_state.dir\n        if required_dir != -1: # Ensure a valid target direction was found\n            while current_dir != required_dir:\n                # Calculate shorter turn (right or left)\n                turn_right_steps = (required_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n                turn_left_steps = (current_dir - required_dir + 4) % 4\n\n                turn_action = action_map['RIGHT'] if turn_right_steps <= turn_left_steps else action_map['LEFT']\n                \n                _reward, done, _observations = env.step(turn_action)\n                actions_taken.append(turn_action)\n                current_state = env._current_state # Update state after turn\n                current_dir = current_state.dir\n                if done:\n                    return actions_taken\n\n        # Now agent is oriented (or was already), perform USE\n        _reward, done, _observations = env.step(action_map['USE'])\n        actions_taken.append(action_map['USE'])\n        # Invalidate the path because the primitive might have been collected or the grid changed\n        current_path_actions = None \n        if done:\n            return actions_taken\n        continue # Successfully used, go to next iteration to re-check inventory\n\n    # 3. Path Planning or Path Following\n    if current_path_actions is None or len(current_path_actions) == 0:\n        # If no path is currently planned or the existing path is exhausted, find a new one\n        \n        current_pos = current_state.pos\n        grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n        queue = deque([(current_pos[0], current_pos[1], [])]) # (x, y, path_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n        visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1])} # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles\n        \n        path_found_by_bfs = None \n        \n        while queue:\n            px, py, path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n            # Check if the current BFS position (px, py) is suitable to be adjacent to the primitive\n            # This means checking the 8 neighbors of (px, py) for the primitive.\n            target_primitive_found_by_bfs = False\n            for dx_nb in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                for dy_nb in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                    if dx_nb == 0 and dy_nb == 0: # Exclude the current BFS position itself\n                        continue\n                    nx_nb, ny_nb = px + dx_nb, py + dy_nb\n                    if _is_valid_pos(nx_nb, ny_nb, grid.shape) and grid[nx_nb, ny_nb, primitive] == 1:\n                        target_primitive_found_by_bfs = True\n                        break\n                if target_primitive_found_by_bfs:\n                    break\n            \n            if target_primitive_found_by_bfs:\n                path_found_by_bfs = path_so_far\n                break # Path found, exit BFS\n                \n            # Explore valid and unvisited neighboring cells for movement\n            for action_val, (dx, dy) in move_deltas.items():\n                next_x, next_y = px + dx, py + dy\n                # Ensure within bounds and not visited\n                if _is_valid_pos(next_x, next_y, grid.shape) and (next_x, next_y) not in visited:\n                    visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n                    queue.append((next_x, next_y, path_so_far + [action_val]))\n        \n        current_path_actions = path_found_by_bfs # Store the computed path for subsequent steps\n\n    # 4. Execute the next action in the pre-computed path\n    action_to_take = None\n    if current_path_actions is not None and len(current_path_actions) > 0:\n        action_to_take = current_path_actions.pop(0) # Take the first step and remove it from the planned path\n    \n    if action_to_take is not None:\n        # Perform the step in the environment\n        _reward, done, _observations = env.step(action_to_take)\n        actions_taken.append(action_to_take)\n        \n        # If the environment indicates the episode is done (e.g., max_steps reached)\n        if done:\n          return actions_taken\n    else:\n        # If no valid action could be determined (e.g., primitive unreachable, or no path found)\n        break\n            \n  return actions_taken", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:46:30.865336", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Define action constants based on CraftLab.action_specs\n  # CraftLab.action_specs: dict mapping DOWN\u21920, UP\u21921, LEFT\u21922, RIGHT\u21923, USE\u21924\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # Define internal direction constants used by CraftState.dir and for grid calculations.\n  # Based on the logic in collect_v1's _get_facing_coords and movement_actions_map,\n  # the internal direction mapping appears to be: 0=UP, 1=RIGHT, 2=DOWN, 3=LEFT.\n  INTERNAL_DIR_UP = 0\n  INTERNAL_DIR_RIGHT = 1\n  INTERNAL_DIR_DOWN = 2\n  INTERNAL_DIR_LEFT = 3\n\n  # Max steps for collection pathfinding. This constant must be defined for the function to run.\n  # A reasonable default to prevent infinite searches in large or complex environments.\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 100 \n\n\n  # Helper function: determines coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n  # This function uses the agent's internal direction representation (INTERNAL_DIR_X).\n  def _get_facing_coords(y, x, internal_direction):\n      \"\"\"Returns the coordinates of the cell directly in front of (y,x) based on agent's facing direction.\"\"\"\n      if internal_direction == INTERNAL_DIR_UP:    return y - 1, x\n      if internal_direction == INTERNAL_DIR_RIGHT: return y, x + 1\n      if internal_direction == INTERNAL_DIR_DOWN:  return y + 1, x\n      if internal_direction == INTERNAL_DIR_LEFT:  return y, x - 1\n      return y, x # Should not be reached with valid directions\n\n  actions_taken = [] # List to store the sequence of actions to be returned\n  \n  # 1. Initialize environment state and perform preliminary checks\n  # Reset the environment to ensure a fresh start and retrieve the initial CraftState.\n  _ = env.reset() # The observation is not needed for pathfinding; we access internal state.\n  current_state = env._current_state # Direct access to the current CraftState instance\n\n  # Verify the primitive is a recognized kind in the world's cookbook.\n  if primitive not in current_state.world.cookbook.kinds:\n      return [] # Unknown primitive, cannot collect.\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already present in the agent's inventory.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return [] # Primitive already collected, no actions needed.\n\n  # Obtain grid dimensions and the agent's initial position and facing direction.\n  full_grid = current_state.features_dict()['features_global']\n  grid_height, grid_width, _ = full_grid.shape\n  start_y, start_x = current_state.pos # Agent's starting Y, X coordinates\n  start_dir = current_state.dir       # Agent's initial facing direction (e.g., INTERNAL_DIR_UP)\n\n  # Check for immediate limits on path length.\n  if MAX_COLLECT_STEPS <= 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Define Impassable Regions for Agent Movement\n  # A set of entity indices representing terrain or objects that the agent cannot traverse.\n  # Start with all non-grabbable items, then specifically remove traversable non-grabbables.\n  impassable_for_movement = set(current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  \n  # Workshops are non-grabbable but typically traversable; remove them from the impassable set.\n  impassable_for_movement.difference_update(current_state.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  # Water (if present and defined) is often an impassable entity.\n  if current_state.world.water_index in current_state.world.kinds:\n      impassable_for_movement.add(current_state.world.water_index)\n\n  # 3. Define Movement Actions and Their Effects on Agent State\n  # Maps each action ID (e.g., ACTION_UP) to a tuple:\n  # (new_internal_direction, delta_y, delta_x) after taking the action.\n  movement_actions_map = {\n      ACTION_UP:    (INTERNAL_DIR_UP, -1, 0),    # Move North, face North\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (INTERNAL_DIR_RIGHT, 0, 1), # Move East, face East\n      ACTION_DOWN:  (INTERNAL_DIR_DOWN, 1, 0),  # Move South, face South\n      ACTION_LEFT:  (INTERNAL_DIR_LEFT, 0, -1)  # Move West, face West\n  }\n\n  # 4. Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to collect the primitive\n  q = collections.deque()\n  # BFS state stores: (current_y, current_x, current_internal_direction, path_of_actions_so_far)\n  q.append((start_y, start_x, start_dir, []))\n\n  # Visited set to prevent revisiting the same (position, direction) state, which avoids cycles\n  # and redundant computation. Facing direction is crucial because ACTION_USE depends on it.\n  visited = {(start_y, start_x, start_dir)} \n\n  path_to_execute = None # This will store the optimal action sequence, including ACTION_USE\n\n  while q:\n      curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir, path = q.popleft()\n\n      # First, check if the primitive can be collected from the current (position, direction) state\n      facing_y, facing_x = _get_facing_coords(curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir)\n\n      # Ensure the facing coordinates are within the grid boundaries\n      if (0 <= facing_y < grid_height and 0 <= facing_x < grid_width):\n          # Check if the primitive exists in the cell the agent is currently facing.\n          if full_grid[facing_y, facing_x, primitive] > 0:\n              candidate_path = path + [ACTION_USE]\n              \n              # If this path is within the allowed step limit, it's a valid solution.\n              # BFS guarantees the first path found is the shortest.\n              if len(candidate_path) <= MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n                  path_to_execute = candidate_path\n                  break # Optimal path found, terminate BFS.\n\n      # Explore neighboring states by applying movement actions\n      for action_move, (next_dir, dy, dx) in movement_actions_map.items():\n          next_y, next_x = curr_y + dy, curr_x + dx\n          \n          # Prune search branches if adding another step exceeds the maximum allowed steps.\n          if len(path) + 1 > MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the proposed next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_y < grid_height and 0 <= next_x < grid_width):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the proposed next cell is traversable (not impassable).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for k_idx in impassable_for_movement:\n              if full_grid[next_y, next_x, k_idx] > 0:\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break\n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue\n          \n          # Check if this (position, direction) state has already been explored.\n          if (next_y, next_x, next_dir) in visited:\n              continue\n\n          # Add the new, valid state to the queue and mark it as visited.\n          visited.add((next_y, next_x, next_dir))\n          q.append((next_y, next_x, next_dir, path + [action_move]))\n    \n  # 5. Execute the found path in the environment\n  if path_to_execute is None:\n      return [] # No valid path found within MAX_COLLECT_STEPS to collect the primitive.\n\n  for action in path_to_execute:\n      actions_taken.append(action)\n      \n      # Take a step in the simulation.\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(action)\n      current_state = env._current_state # Always update the internal state reference.\n\n      # If the primitive is collected after this action, we can stop and return the path.\n      if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n          return actions_taken\n      \n      # If the episode ends prematurely (e.g., max_steps reached) and the goal is not met,\n      # this path effectively failed.\n      if done:\n          if current_state.inventory[primitive] <= 0:\n              return [] # Episode terminated before collection; path failed.\n\n  # Final verification: After executing all actions in the path, confirm collection.\n  # This covers cases where the collection might happen on the very last step.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return actions_taken\n  else:\n      # This case should ideally not be reached if the BFS correctly identified a path\n      # leading to collection, assuming a deterministic environment.\n      return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:46:31.849116", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Define action constants based on CraftLab.action_specs() mapping:\n  # DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3, USE=4\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # Define a maximum number of steps for the BFS to find a path.\n  # This prevents excessively long search times and limits the length of the generated action sequence.\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 100 \n\n  # Helper function defined inside to adhere to the \"only return code that will fit in that function\" rule.\n  def _get_facing_coords(y, x, direction):\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the grid coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n\n      Args:\n          y (int): Agent's current row coordinate.\n          x (int): Agent's current column coordinate.\n          direction (int): Agent's current facing direction (0=Up, 1=Right, 2=Down, 3=Left).\n\n      Returns:\n          tuple[int, int]: (row, column) coordinates of the cell in front.\n      \"\"\"\n      if direction == 0:  # UP\n          return y - 1, x\n      if direction == 1:  # RIGHT\n          return y, x + 1\n      if direction == 2:  # DOWN\n          return y + 1, x\n      if direction == 3:  # LEFT\n          return y, x - 1\n      # Fallback for unexpected direction value, though typically not reached during valid gameplay.\n      return y, x\n\n  actions_taken = []\n\n  # IMPORTANT IMPROVEMENT for v2: Do NOT call env.reset() here.\n  # The `collect` function should compute actions from the *current* state of the environment,\n  # allowing it to be chained with other actions or used as part of a larger plan.\n  # Access the internal CraftState instance directly to get the current state information.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n\n  # Basic validation: Ensure the `primitive` is a recognized entity kind in the world's cookbook.\n  if primitive not in current_state.world.cookbook.kinds:\n      return []\n\n  # Optimization: If the `primitive` is already in the agent's inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve necessary environment information for pathfinding.\n  full_grid = current_state.features_dict()['features_global']\n  grid_height, grid_width, _ = full_grid.shape\n  start_y, start_x = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Use current_state.dir, as env is not reset to init_dir.\n\n  # Determine which entity kinds are impassable for agent movement.\n  # This set will include water (if defined) and any non-grabbable items that are not workshops.\n  impassable_for_movement = set()\n  if current_state.world.water_index in current_state.world.kinds:\n      impassable_for_movement.add(current_state.world.water_index)\n  \n  # Iterate through all non-grabbable indices.\n  # Assume that non-grabbable items that are *not* workshops are actual blockers for movement.\n  # Workshops (e.g., workbench, furnace) are typically traversable even if they cannot be picked up.\n  for k_idx in current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      if k_idx not in current_state.world.workshop_indices:\n          impassable_for_movement.add(k_idx)\n\n  # Define movement actions, their resulting agent direction, and the (dy, dx) grid changes.\n  # The agent's direction automatically updates based on the movement action performed.\n  movement_actions_map = {\n      ACTION_UP:    (0, -1, 0),  # Action UP: results in direction 0 (UP), moves North\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0, 1),   # Action RIGHT: results in direction 1 (RIGHT), moves East\n      ACTION_DOWN:  (2, 1, 0),   # Action DOWN: results in direction 2 (DOWN), moves South\n      ACTION_LEFT:  (3, 0, -1)   # Action LEFT: results in direction 3 (LEFT), moves West\n  }\n\n  q = collections.deque()\n  # BFS queue state: (current_y, current_x, current_direction, path_of_actions_so_far)\n  # Storing the current direction is crucial because `ACTION_USE` is dependent on agent orientation.\n\n  # If the maximum allowed steps for pathfinding is non-positive, no path can be found.\n  if MAX_COLLECT_STEPS <= 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Initialize BFS: Start from the agent's current position and direction with an empty action path.\n  q.append((start_y, start_x, start_dir, []))\n  # Keep track of visited states to prevent redundant exploration and infinite loops in cyclic maps.\n  # A state is defined by (position_y, position_x, direction) because the same grid cell\n  # with a different orientation constitutes a distinct state for the purpose of `ACTION_USE`.\n  visited = {(start_y, start_x, start_dir)}\n\n  path_to_execute = None  # This variable will store the final sequence of actions if a valid path is found.\n\n  # --- Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest action sequence to collect the primitive ---\n  while q:\n      curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir, path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Optimization: If the current path length already exceeds MAX_COLLECT_STEPS,\n      # this branch cannot lead to a valid solution within the specified limits.\n      if len(path) > MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n          continue\n\n      # Calculate the coordinates of the grid cell that the agent is currently facing.\n      facing_y, facing_x = _get_facing_coords(curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir)\n\n      # Check if the facing cell is within grid boundaries and contains the target primitive.\n      if (0 <= facing_y < grid_height and 0 <= facing_x < grid_width and\n          full_grid[facing_y, facing_x, primitive] > 0):\n\n          # We've found a position and orientation from which `ACTION_USE` can be performed successfully.\n          candidate_path = path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n          # Ensure the complete path (including the final `ACTION_USE`) is within the step limit.\n          if len(candidate_path) <= MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n              path_to_execute = candidate_path\n              # Since BFS guarantees finding the shortest path first, we can stop as soon as one is found.\n              break # Exit the BFS loop\n\n      # Explore all possible next states from the current state (curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir).\n      # This involves trying each possible movement action.\n      for action_move, (next_dir, dy, dx) in movement_actions_map.items():\n          next_y, next_x = curr_y + dy, curr_x + dx\n\n          # Pruning: If adding this move makes the path too long, skip this potential step.\n          if len(path) + 1 > MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the proposed next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_y < grid_height and 0 <= next_x < grid_width):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the proposed next cell is traversable based on the `impassable_for_movement` set.\n          is_traversable = True\n          for k_idx in impassable_for_movement:\n              if full_grid[next_y, next_x, k_idx] > 0:\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break\n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue\n\n          # Check if this new (position, direction) state has already been visited.\n          # This prevents redundant work and infinite loops in cyclic environments.\n          if (next_y, next_x, next_dir) in visited:\n              continue\n\n          # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue for further exploration.\n          visited.add((next_y, next_x, next_dir))\n          q.append((next_y, next_x, next_dir, path + [action_move]))\n\n  # --- Execute the found path (if any) and monitor for successful collection ---\n  if path_to_execute is None:\n      # If no valid path was found within the step limit, return an empty list.\n      return []\n\n  for action in path_to_execute:\n      actions_taken.append(action)\n      # Perform the action in the environment.\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(action)\n      # Update the internal state reference after each step to reflect the current environment.\n      current_state = env._current_state\n\n      # Check for early termination of the episode without successfully collecting the primitive.\n      # This ensures robustness if the environment ends due to other reasons (e.g., `max_steps` reached\n      # by `CraftLab`) before the collection is complete.\n      if done and current_state.inventory[primitive] <= 0:\n          return []  # Episode ended, but the goal was not satisfied.\n\n      # If the primitive is collected, we can stop executing the remaining actions in the path.\n      if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n          return actions_taken\n\n  # Final check after executing all actions in the `path_to_execute`.\n  # This handles cases where the primitive is collected on the very last action of the path.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return actions_taken\n  else:\n      # If the full path was executed but the primitive was not collected,\n      # it indicates a discrepancy (e.g., the primitive disappeared dynamically),\n      # which should ideally not happen if the BFS correctly found a path.\n      return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:47:58.337912", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    actions_to_collect = []\n\n    # Get action mappings dynamically from the environment\n    action_spec = env.action_specs()\n    ACTION_DOWN = action_spec['DOWN']\n    ACTION_UP = action_spec['UP']\n    ACTION_LEFT = action_spec['LEFT']\n    ACTION_RIGHT = action_spec['RIGHT']\n    ACTION_USE = action_spec['USE']\n\n    # Set a safety limit for iterations to prevent infinite loops in complex scenarios\n    # or if the primitive is unreachable/non-existent.\n    MAX_COLLECTION_STEPS = 200 \n\n    for _ in range(MAX_COLLECTION_STEPS):\n        obs = env.observations()\n        inventory = obs['features_dict']['inventory']\n\n        # Check if the primitive is already collected\n        if inventory[primitive] > 0:\n            break # Goal achieved, stop collecting\n\n        # Access the internal CraftState for precise position and grid info.\n        # This direct access is assumed to be permissible for this problem context\n        # as a pragmatic approach given the provided class structure.\n        current_state = env._current_state\n        agent_y, agent_x = current_state.pos\n        grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global'] # Full global grid view\n\n        # 1. Check if agent is already next to the primitive\n        # CraftState.next_to checks if any cell in the 3x3 neighborhood contains the kind.\n        # We assume that the 'USE' action collects an item if the agent is in this neighborhood.\n        if current_state.next_to(primitive):\n            actions_to_collect.append(ACTION_USE)\n            reward, done, _ = env.step(ACTION_USE) # Apply the action\n            if done: # Check if environment terminated (e.g., max_steps reached or goal met)\n                # If done and primitive still not collected, it means collection failed or timed out.\n                if obs['features_dict']['inventory'][primitive] == 0: # Re-check inventory after step\n                    return [] # Collection failed, return actions taken so far\n            continue # Re-evaluate state after taking USE action\n\n        # 2. If not next to the primitive, find its closest location and path towards an adjacent cell.\n        primitive_locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive] == 1)\n\n        if len(primitive_locations) == 0:\n            # Primitive not found on the map. Cannot collect.\n            return []\n\n        closest_adj_pos = None\n        min_distance = float('inf')\n\n        # Iterate over all primitive locations to find the one closest to the agent\n        # by considering its 4-directional adjacent cells.\n        for prim_y, prim_x in primitive_locations:\n            # Define potential adjacent cells (up, down, left, right)\n            potential_adjacents = [\n                (prim_y - 1, prim_x), (prim_y + 1, prim_x),\n                (prim_y, prim_x - 1), (prim_y, prim_x + 1)\n            ]\n            for adj_y, adj_x in potential_adjacents:\n                # Ensure the adjacent cell is within grid bounds\n                if 0 <= adj_y < grid.shape[0] and 0 <= adj_x < grid.shape[1]:\n                    # Calculate Manhattan distance from agent's current position to this adjacent cell\n                    dist = abs(agent_y - adj_y) + abs(agent_x - adj_x)\n                    if dist < min_distance:\n                        min_distance = dist\n                        closest_adj_pos = (adj_y, adj_x)\n\n        if closest_adj_pos is None:\n            # This case implies no valid adjacent cell was found (e.g., surrounded by unpassable terrain).\n            return []\n\n        target_y, target_x = closest_adj_pos\n\n        # Determine the next greedy movement action to take towards the target adjacent cell.\n        action_to_take = None\n        # Prioritize horizontal movement to minimize steps for Manhattan distance\n        if agent_x < target_x:\n            action_to_take = ACTION_RIGHT\n        elif agent_x > target_x:\n            action_to_take = ACTION_LEFT\n        # If horizontal position is aligned, move vertically\n        elif agent_y < target_y:\n            action_to_take = ACTION_DOWN\n        elif agent_y > target_y:\n            action_to_take = ACTION_UP\n        \n        # If no movement action is determined, it means the agent is already at the target_adj_pos.\n        # This scenario should be caught by the `next_to` check at the beginning of the loop.\n        # If it reaches here, it might indicate an unmovable state or an issue.\n        if action_to_take is None:\n            break # Exit loop if no further actions can be determined for movement\n\n        # Take the determined movement action\n        actions_to_collect.append(action_to_take)\n        reward, done, _ = env.step(action_to_take) # Apply action and update environment state\n\n        if done: # If the environment signals done (e.g., max_steps reached by CraftLab)\n            break # Stop trying to collect, as episode has ended\n\n    return actions_to_collect", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:47:59.334094", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  inventory = current_state.inventory\n  world = env.world # CraftWorld instance\n\n  # Check if primitive is already collected\n  if inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Grid dimensions\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # BFS setup\n  # Queue stores (position, path_taken)\n  q = deque([(current_pos, [])])\n  visited = {current_pos}\n\n  # Action to (dx, dy) mapping\n  # Assumes (x, y) coordinates where x is horizontal, y is vertical\n  # UP: (0, -1) means y decreases\n  # DOWN: (0, 1) means y increases\n  # LEFT: (-1, 0) means x decreases\n  # RIGHT: (1, 0) means x increases\n  ACTION_DELTAS = [\n      (env_factory.UP, 0, -1),\n      (env_factory.DOWN, 0, 1),\n      (env_factory.LEFT, -1, 0),\n      (env_factory.RIGHT, 1, 0),\n  ]\n\n  # BFS loop\n  while q:\n    (px, py), path = q.popleft()\n\n    # Check if any adjacent cell contains the primitive\n    # We need to be adjacent to 'use' it\n    for action, dx, dy in ACTION_DELTAS:\n      nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n\n      # Check bounds\n      if not (0 <= nx < grid_width and 0 <= ny < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # Check if this neighbor cell contains the primitive\n      if grid[nx, ny, primitive] == 1:\n        # We found the primitive adjacent to (px, py)\n        # The path to reach (px, py) is 'path'.\n        # The final action needed is 'USE'.\n        return path + [env_factory.USE]\n\n    # If not adjacent to the primitive, explore neighbors for movement\n    for action, dx, dy in ACTION_DELTAS:\n      next_pos = (px + dx, py + dy)\n\n      # Check bounds\n      if not (0 <= next_pos[0] < grid_width and 0 <= next_pos[1] < grid_height):\n        continue\n\n      # Check if already visited\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # Passability check (simple: assume all cells are passable unless they are\n      # non-grabbable items that are not the target primitive itself.\n      # For this problem, let's assume agent can move into empty cells or cells\n      # containing grabbable items (that are not the target).\n      # A more robust check might involve checking for `world.non_grabbable_indices`\n      # if they occupy the entire cell and are impassable, like water.\n      # For now, we assume simple movement.\n      \n      visited.add(next_pos)\n      q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))\n\n  # If no path found (primitive unreachable or not on grid)\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:49:03.237128", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n  from enum import IntEnum\n\n  # Define actions based on CraftLab.action_specs() mapping:\n  # DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3, USE=4\n  class Action(IntEnum):\n      DOWN = 0\n      UP = 1\n      LEFT = 2\n      RIGHT = 3\n      USE = 4\n\n  # Agent directions (matches CraftState.dir attribute: 0=East, 1=South, 2=West, 3=North)\n  DIR_EAST = 0\n  DIR_SOUTH = 1\n  DIR_WEST = 2\n  DIR_NORTH = 3\n\n  # Mapping of a target's relative coordinates (dy, dx) from the agent to the\n  # required agent facing direction to collect that target via ACTION_USE.\n  # This focuses on cardinal directions, as ACTION_USE typically applies to what's directly in front.\n  # Format: (relative_dy, relative_dx): required_agent_direction\n  RELATIVE_TO_REQUIRED_DIR = {\n      (0, 1): DIR_EAST,   # Target is to the East (+1 in x), agent must face East (DIR_EAST)\n      (1, 0): DIR_SOUTH,  # Target is to the South (+1 in y), agent must face South (DIR_SOUTH)\n      (0, -1): DIR_WEST,  # Target is to the West (-1 in x), agent must face West (DIR_WEST)\n      (-1, 0): DIR_NORTH  # Target is to the North (-1 in y), agent must face North (DIR_NORTH)\n  }\n\n  # Mapping of movement actions to (dy, dx, resulting_direction_after_move).\n  # The resulting_direction is the direction the agent faces after performing the move.\n  MOVEMENT_ACTIONS = {\n      Action.UP:    (-1, 0, DIR_NORTH),  # Move North (dy=-1), face North\n      Action.DOWN:  (1, 0, DIR_SOUTH),   # Move South (dy=+1), face South\n      Action.LEFT:  (0, -1, DIR_WEST),   # Move West (dx=-1), face West\n      Action.RIGHT: (0, 1, DIR_EAST)    # Move East (dx=+1), face East\n  }\n\n  # Maximum number of actions allowed for collection, including movements and the final USE.\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 100\n\n  actions_taken = []\n\n  # Access the underlying CraftState instance to get the current state information.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n\n  # Basic validation: Ensure the `primitive` is a recognized entity kind in the world's cookbook.\n  if primitive not in current_state.world.cookbook.kinds:\n      return []\n\n  # Optimization: If the `primitive` is already in the agent's inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve necessary environment information for pathfinding.\n  # Use the global grid view for comprehensive pathfinding.\n  full_grid = current_state.features_dict()['features_global']\n  grid_height, grid_width, _ = full_grid.shape\n  start_y, start_x = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir\n\n  # Determine which entity kinds are impassable for agent movement.\n  impassable_for_movement = set()\n  \n  # Water is typically impassable.\n  if current_state.world.water_index in current_state.world.kinds:\n      impassable_for_movement.add(current_state.world.water_index)\n  \n  # Non-grabbable entities that are NOT workshops are usually impassable for movement.\n  # Workshops (e.g., workbench, furnace) are often traversable even if non-grabbable.\n  for k_idx in current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      if k_idx not in current_state.world.workshop_indices:\n          impassable_for_movement.add(k_idx)\n\n  # Pre-compute positions of the target primitive on the grid for quick lookup during BFS.\n  primitive_locations = set()\n  for y in range(grid_height):\n      for x in range(grid_width):\n          if full_grid[y, x, primitive] > 0:\n              primitive_locations.add((y, x))\n\n  # If the primitive isn't on the grid at all, no path can be found.\n  if not primitive_locations:\n      return []\n\n  q = collections.deque()\n  # BFS queue state: (current_y, current_x, current_direction, path_of_actions_so_far)\n  # The direction (curr_dir) is crucial because ACTION_USE depends on agent orientation.\n  q.append((start_y, start_x, start_dir, []))\n\n  # Keep track of visited states (position + orientation) to prevent redundant exploration and cycles.\n  visited = {(start_y, start_x, start_dir)}\n\n  path_to_execute = None  # This will store the final sequence of actions if a valid path is found.\n\n  # --- Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest action sequence to collect the primitive ---\n  while q:\n      curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir, path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Pruning: If the current path length already equals or exceeds MAX_COLLECT_STEPS,\n      # this path (or any further extension of it) cannot be a valid solution within limits.\n      # We use >= because the final ACTION_USE needs one step too.\n      if len(path) >= MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n          continue\n\n      # Check if the primitive is cardinally adjacent and collectable from the current state.\n      for (rel_dy, rel_dx), required_dir in RELATIVE_TO_REQUIRED_DIR.items():\n          adj_y, adj_x = curr_y + rel_dy, curr_x + rel_dx\n\n          # Check if the adjacent cell is within grid boundaries, contains the primitive,\n          # and the agent is currently facing the correct direction to use on it.\n          if (0 <= adj_y < grid_height and 0 <= adj_x < grid_width and\n              (adj_y, adj_x) in primitive_locations and\n              curr_dir == required_dir):\n              \n              candidate_path = path + [Action.USE]\n\n              # Ensure the complete path (including the final ACTION_USE) is within the step limit.\n              if len(candidate_path) <= MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n                  path_to_execute = candidate_path\n                  break # Found the shortest path, exit the inner loop\n      \n      if path_to_execute: # If a valid path was found and assigned, break the outer BFS loop too.\n          break\n\n      # Explore all possible next states from the current state (curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir).\n      # This involves trying each possible movement action.\n      for action_move, (dy_move, dx_move, new_dir_after_move) in MOVEMENT_ACTIONS.items():\n          next_y, next_x = curr_y + dy_move, curr_x + dx_move\n\n          # Check if the proposed next position is within the grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_y < grid_height and 0 <= next_x < grid_width):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the proposed next cell is traversable based on `impassable_for_movement`.\n          is_traversable = True\n          for k_idx in impassable_for_movement:\n              if full_grid[next_y, next_x, k_idx] > 0:\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break\n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue\n\n          # Check if this new (position, direction) state has already been visited.\n          if (next_y, next_x, new_dir_after_move) in visited:\n              continue\n\n          # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue for further exploration.\n          visited.add((next_y, next_x, new_dir_after_move))\n          q.append((next_y, next_x, new_dir_after_move, path + [action_move]))\n\n  # --- Execute the found path (if any) and monitor for successful collection ---\n  if path_to_execute is None:\n      # If no valid path was found within the step limit, return an empty list.\n      return []\n\n  for action in path_to_execute:\n      actions_taken.append(action)\n      \n      # Perform the action in the environment.\n      _, done, _ = env.step(action)\n      \n      # Update the internal state reference after each step to reflect the current environment.\n      current_state = env._current_state\n\n      # Check for early termination of the episode without successfully collecting the primitive.\n      if done and current_state.inventory[primitive] <= 0:\n          return []  # Episode ended, but the goal was not satisfied.\n\n      # If the primitive is collected, we can stop executing the remaining actions in the path.\n      if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n          return actions_taken\n\n  # Final check after executing all actions in the `path_to_execute`.\n  # This handles cases where the primitive is collected on the very last action of the path.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return actions_taken\n  else:\n      # This scenario should ideally not be reached if the BFS successfully found a path\n      # that leads to collection. It might indicate a dynamic change in the environment\n      # (e.g., primitive disappeared) or a mismatch in simulation.\n      return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:49:04.267931", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n  from enum import IntEnum\n\n  # Define action constants based on CraftLab.action_specs() mapping:\n  # DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3, USE=4\n  class Action(IntEnum):\n      DOWN = 0\n      UP = 1\n      LEFT = 2\n      RIGHT = 3\n      USE = 4\n\n  # Define CraftState agent directions based on its documentation:\n  # 0=East, 1=South, 2=West, 3=North\n  class AgentDirection(IntEnum):\n      EAST = 0\n      SOUTH = 1\n      WEST = 2\n      NORTH = 3\n\n  # Define a maximum number of steps for the BFS to find a path and for action execution.\n  # This prevents excessively long search times and limits the length of the generated action sequence.\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 100\n\n  # Helper function: Determines the grid cell coordinates directly in front of the agent.\n  def _get_facing_coords(y, x, direction):\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the grid coordinates (row, col) of the cell directly in front of the agent,\n      based on the agent's current position and facing direction (CraftState.dir).\n      \"\"\"\n      if direction == AgentDirection.EAST:\n          return y, x + 1\n      elif direction == AgentDirection.SOUTH:\n          return y + 1, x\n      elif direction == AgentDirection.WEST:\n          return y, x - 1\n      elif direction == AgentDirection.NORTH:\n          return y - 1, x\n      # Should not be reached with valid direction values\n      return y, x\n\n  actions_taken = [] # List to store the sequence of actions to be returned.\n\n  # Access the current state of the environment directly.\n  # The `collect` function is designed to work from the current environment state,\n  # not to reset the environment first.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n\n  # Pre-check 1: Validate if the primitive ID is known in the world's cookbook.\n  if primitive not in current_state.world.cookbook.kinds:\n      return []\n\n  # Pre-check 2: If the primitive is already in the agent's inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Retrieve essential environment details from the current state for pathfinding.\n  full_grid = current_state.features_dict()['features_global']\n  grid_height, grid_width, _ = full_grid.shape\n  start_y, start_x = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction\n\n  # Identify impassable entity kinds for agent movement.\n  # This set includes \"water\" (if defined) and any \"non-grabbable\" items that are\n  # NOT considered \"workshops\" (as workshops are typically traversable).\n  impassable_for_movement = set()\n  if current_state.world.water_index in current_state.world.kinds:\n      impassable_for_movement.add(current_state.world.water_index)\n\n  for k_idx in current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      if k_idx not in current_state.world.workshop_indices:\n          impassable_for_movement.add(k_idx)\n\n  # Define mapping from movement actions to their effects:\n  # (resulting_agent_direction, delta_y, delta_x)\n  # This assumes that movement actions inherently reorient the agent to face the\n  # direction of movement.\n  movement_actions_map = {\n      Action.UP:    (AgentDirection.NORTH, -1, 0), # Move North (dy=-1, dx=0), resulting dir: NORTH\n      Action.DOWN:  (AgentDirection.SOUTH, 1, 0),  # Move South (dy=1, dx=0), resulting dir: SOUTH\n      Action.LEFT:  (AgentDirection.WEST, 0, -1),  # Move West (dy=0, dx=-1), resulting dir: WEST\n      Action.RIGHT: (AgentDirection.EAST, 0, 1)   # Move East (dy=0, dx=1), resulting dir: EAST\n  }\n\n  q = collections.deque()\n  # BFS queue state: (current_y, current_x, current_direction, path_of_actions_so_far)\n  # Storing the direction is crucial because `Action.USE` depends on agent orientation.\n\n  # Initialize BFS from the agent's current state.\n  q.append((start_y, start_x, start_dir, []))\n  # Keep track of visited states to prevent redundant exploration and infinite loops.\n  # A state is defined by (position_y, position_x, direction).\n  visited = {(start_y, start_x, start_dir)}\n\n  path_to_execute = None # This will store the final optimal action sequence found by BFS.\n\n  # --- Breadth-First Search (BFS) for the shortest path to collect the primitive ---\n  while q:\n      curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir, path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Pruning: If the current path length already exceeds the maximum allowed steps,\n      # this branch cannot lead to a valid solution within limits.\n      if len(path) > MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n          continue\n\n      # Check if the primitive is collectable from the current position and orientation.\n      # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      facing_y, facing_x = _get_facing_coords(curr_y, curr_x, curr_dir)\n\n      # Verify if the facing cell is within bounds and contains the target primitive.\n      if (0 <= facing_y < grid_height and 0 <= facing_x < grid_width and\n          full_grid[facing_y, facing_x, primitive] > 0):\n          \n          # Found a state where the agent is correctly positioned and oriented to collect.\n          candidate_path = path + [Action.USE] # Append the final USE action.\n\n          # Ensure the complete path (including USE) is within the step limit.\n          if len(candidate_path) <= MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n              path_to_execute = candidate_path\n              break # BFS guarantees the shortest path first, so we can stop.\n\n      # Explore all possible next states reachable by movement actions.\n      for action_move, (next_dir, dy, dx) in movement_actions_map.items():\n          next_y, next_x = curr_y + dy, curr_x + dx\n\n          # Pruning: If adding this move makes the path too long, skip.\n          if len(path) + 1 > MAX_COLLECT_STEPS:\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_y < grid_height and 0 <= next_x < grid_width):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the next cell is traversable (not blocked by impassable entities).\n          is_traversable = True\n          for k_idx in impassable_for_movement:\n              if full_grid[next_y, next_x, k_idx] > 0:\n                  is_traversable = False\n                  break\n          if not is_traversable:\n              continue\n\n          # Check if this new state (position + direction) has already been visited.\n          if (next_y, next_x, next_dir) in visited:\n              continue\n\n          # If all checks pass, add the new state to the queue for further exploration.\n          visited.add((next_y, next_x, next_dir))\n          q.append((next_y, next_x, next_dir, path + [action_move]))\n\n  # --- Execute the found path (if any) and monitor for successful collection ---\n  if path_to_execute is None:\n      # If no valid path was found within the step limit, return an empty list.\n      return []\n\n  for action in path_to_execute:\n      actions_taken.append(action)\n      # Perform the action in the environment.\n      # We ignore reward for this function's purpose, but check `done` status.\n      _, done, _ = env.step(action)\n      # Update the internal state reference after each step to reflect current environment.\n      current_state = env._current_state\n\n      # Check for early termination of the episode (e.g., max_steps reached)\n      # *before* the primitive was successfully collected.\n      if done and current_state.inventory[primitive] <= 0:\n          return [] # Episode ended, but goal not satisfied.\n\n      # If the primitive is collected at any point during path execution, we're done.\n      if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n          return actions_taken\n\n  # Final check after executing all actions in the planned path.\n  # This covers the case where the primitive is collected on the very last action.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return actions_taken\n  else:\n      # If the full path was executed but the primitive was not collected,\n      # it implies a discrepancy (e.g., primitive disappeared, or initial grid\n      # state for BFS was inaccurate, or a tool was needed not accounted for).\n      return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:50:43.953668", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Constants for actions as defined in CraftLab.action_specs\n    _DOWN = 0\n    _UP = 1\n    _LEFT = 2\n    _RIGHT = 3\n    _USE = 4\n\n    # Get the current state from the environment\n    # env is a CraftLab instance, _current_state is a CraftState instance\n    state = env._current_state\n\n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already collected\n    if state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    grid = state.grid\n    current_x, current_y = state.pos\n    grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n    # 2. Find the closest primitive's location\n    target_px, target_py = -1, -1\n    min_dist = float('inf')\n\n    for x in range(grid_width):\n        for y in range(grid_height):\n            # Check if the primitive exists at this grid cell\n            if grid[x, y, primitive] > 0:\n                # Calculate Manhattan distance from current agent position\n                dist = abs(x - current_x) + abs(y - current_y)\n                if dist < min_dist:\n                    min_dist = dist\n                    target_px = x\n                    target_py = y\n    \n    # If the primitive was not found anywhere on the grid, return an empty list\n    if target_px == -1:\n        return []\n\n    # Helper function to check if the agent is in a position to collect.\n    # This means the target item is either on the same cell as the agent\n    # or in an immediately adjacent (orthogonal) cell.\n    def is_collectable_from(agent_x, agent_y, target_x, target_y):\n        return abs(agent_x - target_x) + abs(agent_y - target_y) <= 1\n\n    actions = []\n    sim_x, sim_y = current_x, current_y # Simulate agent's position\n\n    # 3. Generate actions to move to a collectable position\n    # The loop continues as long as the simulated agent is not adjacent to or on the target cell\n    while not is_collectable_from(sim_x, sim_y, target_px, target_py):\n        dx = target_px - sim_x\n        dy = target_py - sim_y\n\n        action_to_take = -1\n\n        # Prioritize movement along the axis with the larger difference\n        # This creates a more direct, L-shaped path\n        if abs(dx) >= abs(dy):\n            if dx > 0:\n                action_to_take = _RIGHT\n                sim_x += 1\n            elif dx < 0:\n                action_to_take = _LEFT\n                sim_x -= 1\n            # If dx is 0, then we must move along y\n            else:\n                if dy > 0:\n                    action_to_take = _DOWN\n                    sim_y += 1\n                elif dy < 0:\n                    action_to_take = _UP\n                    sim_y -= 1\n        else: # abs(dy) > abs(dx)\n            if dy > 0:\n                action_to_take = _DOWN\n                sim_y += 1\n            elif dy < 0:\n                action_to_take = _UP\n                sim_y -= 1\n            # If dy is 0, then we must move along x\n            else:\n                if dx > 0:\n                    action_to_take = _RIGHT\n                    sim_x += 1\n                elif dx < 0:\n                    action_to_take = _LEFT\n                    sim_x -= 1\n        \n        # Append the determined movement action\n        if action_to_take != -1: # Ensure an action was chosen (should always be if not yet collectable)\n            actions.append(action_to_take)\n        else:\n            # This scenario implies the agent is stuck or target is unreachable,\n            # which is not expected in this simple greedy pathfinding.\n            break \n            \n    # 4. Once in a collectable position, add the USE action\n    actions.append(_USE)\n\n    return actions", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:50:44.027707", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Action constants (from CraftLab.action_specs)\n    ACTION_DOWN = 0\n    ACTION_UP = 1\n    ACTION_LEFT = 2\n    ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n    ACTION_USE = 4\n\n    # Direction constants (assuming 0:North, 1:East, 2:South, 3:West)\n    DIR_NORTH = 0\n    DIR_EAST = 1\n    DIR_SOUTH = 2\n    DIR_WEST = 3\n\n    # Delta for moving in each direction (row, col)\n    # Assuming (0,0) is top-left, row increases downwards, col increases rightwards\n    DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n        DIR_NORTH: (-1, 0),  # Up\n        DIR_EAST: (0, 1),    # Right\n        DIR_SOUTH: (1, 0),   # Down\n        DIR_WEST: (0, -1)    # Left\n    }\n\n    # Helper function to get actions needed to face a target\n    def _get_actions_to_face(current_pos, current_dir, target_pos):\n        actions = []\n        dr = target_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n        dc = target_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n\n        target_dir = -1\n        if dr == -1 and dc == 0:  # Target is North\n            target_dir = DIR_NORTH\n        elif dr == 1 and dc == 0:   # Target is South\n            target_dir = DIR_SOUTH\n        elif dr == 0 and dc == 1:   # Target is East\n            target_dir = DIR_EAST\n        elif dr == 0 and dc == -1:  # Target is West\n            target_dir = DIR_WEST\n        \n        if target_dir == -1: # Not an orthogonal neighbor\n            return []\n\n        diff = (target_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n        if diff == 0: \n            pass # Already facing\n        elif diff == 1: # 1 turn clockwise (RIGHT)\n            actions.append(ACTION_RIGHT)\n        elif diff == 2: # 2 turns (e.g., RIGHT twice)\n            actions.append(ACTION_RIGHT)\n            actions.append(ACTION_RIGHT)\n        elif diff == 3: # 1 turn counter-clockwise (LEFT)\n            actions.append(ACTION_LEFT)\n        return actions\n\n    initial_state = env._current_state\n    initial_pos = initial_state.pos\n    initial_dir = initial_state.dir\n    grid = initial_state.grid\n\n    n_rows, n_cols, _ = grid.shape\n    \n    is_grabbable = primitive in env.world.grabbable_indices\n    is_non_grabbable = primitive in env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n    primitive_locations = []\n    for r in range(n_rows):\n        for c in range(n_cols):\n            if grid[r, c, primitive] > 0:\n                primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n    \n    if not primitive_locations:\n        return []\n\n    q = collections.deque([(initial_pos[0], initial_pos[1], initial_dir, [])]) # (r, c, dir, path_actions)\n    visited = set([(initial_pos[0], initial_pos[1], initial_dir)])\n\n    final_path_actions = []\n    target_primitive_location = None\n\n    while q:\n        r, c, d, path_actions = q.popleft()\n        \n        goal_found = False\n\n        if is_grabbable:\n            if (r, c) in primitive_locations:\n                final_path_actions = list(path_actions)\n                goal_found = True\n                \n        elif is_non_grabbable:\n            # Check orthogonal neighbors of (r, c) for a primitive_location\n            adj_deltas = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)] # N, S, W, E\n            for dr_adj, dc_adj in adj_deltas:\n                adj_r, adj_c = r + dr_adj, c + dc_adj\n                if (adj_r, adj_c) in primitive_locations:\n                    final_path_actions = list(path_actions)\n                    target_primitive_location = (adj_r, adj_c)\n                    goal_found = True\n                    break\n        \n        if goal_found:\n            if is_non_grabbable:\n                actions_to_face = _get_actions_to_face((r, c), d, target_primitive_location)\n                final_path_actions.extend(actions_to_face)\n                final_path_actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n            \n            return final_path_actions\n\n        # Explore neighbors (movements and turns)\n        # 1. Try moving forward\n        dr_move, dc_move = DIR_TO_DELTA[d]\n        next_r, next_c = r + dr_move, c + dc_move\n        \n        if 0 <= next_r < n_rows and 0 <= next_c < n_cols:\n            is_blocked = False\n            for k_idx in env.world.environment: # Check if the next cell contains an environment (obstacle) item\n                if grid[next_r, next_c, k_idx] > 0:\n                    is_blocked = True\n                    break\n            \n            # An additional check: If the target primitive is non-grabbable, we cannot walk onto its cell.\n            # This is implicitly handled: if `primitive` is `is_non_grabbable`, it's in `env.world.environment`,\n            # so `is_blocked` would be true if `next_r, next_c` contains `primitive`.\n            # So, the `is_blocked` check covers walking into any `environment` item, including non-grabbable primitives.\n\n            if not is_blocked:\n                if (next_r, next_c, d) not in visited:\n                    new_path = list(path_actions)\n                    new_path.append(ACTION_UP)\n                    visited.add((next_r, next_c, d))\n                    q.append((next_r, next_c, d, new_path))\n\n        # 2. Try turning left\n        new_d_left = (d - 1 + 4) % 4\n        if (r, c, new_d_left) not in visited:\n            new_path = list(path_actions)\n            new_path.append(ACTION_LEFT)\n            visited.add((r, c, new_d_left))\n            q.append((r, c, new_d_left, new_path))\n\n        # 3. Try turning right\n        new_d_right = (d + 1) % 4\n        if (r, c, new_d_right) not in visited:\n            new_path = list(path_actions)\n            new_path.append(ACTION_RIGHT)\n            visited.add((r, c, new_d_right))\n            q.append((r, c, new_d_right, new_path))\n\n    # If BFS completes without finding a path\n    return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:52:05.259778", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # 1. Check current inventory: If primitive is already collected, return empty list.\n  obs = env.observations()\n  inventory = obs['features_dict']['inventory']\n  if inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n  current_pos = tuple(obs['features_dict']['pos'].astype(int))\n  rows, cols, n_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Get non-grabbable indices from the world to identify obstacles.\n  # `env` is a CraftLab instance. `env.world` is a CraftWorld instance.\n  # `env.world.non_grabbable_indices` is a set of integer indices.\n  non_grabbable_obstacles = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Movement deltas for (dr, dc) corresponding to actions\n  MOVE_DELTAS = {\n      env_factory.UP: (-1, 0),\n      env_factory.DOWN: (1, 0),\n      env_factory.LEFT: (0, -1),\n      env_factory.RIGHT: (0, 1),\n  }\n\n  # 2. Find all target positions on the grid where the primitive exists.\n  target_cells = []\n  for r in range(rows):\n    for c in range(cols):\n      # Check if this cell contains the primitive. Assuming one-hot encoding (value is 1).\n      if grid[r, c, primitive] == 1:\n        target_cells.append((r, c))\n\n  if not target_cells:\n    # Primitive not found on the grid. Cannot collect.\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Define all cells from which the 'USE' action can collect the primitive.\n  # The 'USE' action works for items in a 3x3 neighborhood (as per CraftState.next_to).\n  use_reach_cells = set()\n  for tr, tc in target_cells:\n    for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:  # relative row delta\n      for dc in [-1, 0, 1]:  # relative col delta\n        r_reach, c_reach = tr + dr, tc + dc\n        # Ensure the reachable cell is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= r_reach < rows and 0 <= c_reach < cols:\n          use_reach_cells.add((r_reach, c_reach))\n\n  # 4. BFS to find the shortest path to any `use_reach_cell`.\n  # Queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])])\n  visited = {current_pos}  # Set of visited positions\n\n  while q:\n    curr_pos, curr_actions = q.popleft()\n\n    # If current position is one of the cells from which 'USE' can be applied\n    if curr_pos in use_reach_cells:\n      return curr_actions + [env_factory.USE]  # Return path + USE action\n\n    # Explore neighbors\n    for action_val, (dr, dc) in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n      next_r, next_c = curr_pos[0] + dr, curr_pos[1] + dc\n      next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n      # Boundary check\n      if not (0 <= next_r < rows and 0 <= next_c < cols):\n        continue\n\n      # Check if already visited\n      if next_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # Obstacle check: A cell is considered an obstacle if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n      is_obstacle = False\n      for kind_idx in non_grabbable_obstacles:\n        # Assuming grid values are one-hot (0 or 1).\n        if grid[next_r, next_c, kind_idx] == 1:\n          is_obstacle = True\n          break\n\n      if not is_obstacle:\n        visited.add(next_pos)\n        q.append((next_pos, curr_actions + [action_val]))\n\n  # If BFS completes and no path was found to any reachable cell\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:52:06.232491", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Action constants (assuming these are globally defined or common knowledge in this context)\n  # As per problem description/typical DMLab envs:\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  # Direction constants for agent's `dir` attribute (0:North, 1:East, 2:South, 3:West)\n  NORTH = 0\n  EAST = 1\n  SOUTH = 2\n  WEST = 3\n\n  # Movement deltas for actions (dr, dc)\n  _ACTION_TO_DELTA = {\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1)\n  }\n\n  # Mapping from (current_dir, desired_dir) to list of turning actions\n  # Assumes agent's direction *does not* change during cardinal movements (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n  # Only explicit turn actions (LEFT, RIGHT) change direction.\n  _TURN_ACTIONS_MAP = {\n      (NORTH, NORTH): [],\n      (NORTH, EAST): [RIGHT],\n      (NORTH, SOUTH): [RIGHT, RIGHT], # Two right turns to face opposite\n      (NORTH, WEST): [LEFT],\n\n      (EAST, NORTH): [LEFT],\n      (EAST, EAST): [],\n      (EAST, SOUTH): [RIGHT],\n      (EAST, WEST): [RIGHT, RIGHT],\n\n      (SOUTH, NORTH): [RIGHT, RIGHT],\n      (SOUTH, EAST): [LEFT],\n      (SOUTH, SOUTH): [],\n      (SOUTH, WEST): [RIGHT],\n\n      (WEST, NORTH): [RIGHT],\n      (WEST, EAST): [RIGHT, RIGHT],\n      (WEST, SOUTH): [LEFT],\n      (WEST, WEST): []\n  }\n\n  # 1. Check if primitive is already in inventory\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  current_pos = current_state.pos\n  initial_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's direction before any actions\n  world = env.world\n  \n  height, width, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Define what constitutes an impassable cell for movement\n  # Assuming non_grabbable_indices (environment objects, walls, etc.) are impassable\n  impassable_kinds = world.non_grabbable_indices\n  \n  def is_walkable(r, c):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a cell (r, c) is within bounds and does not contain impassable objects.\"\"\"\n    if not (0 <= r < height and 0 <= c < width):\n      return False # Out of bounds\n    # A cell is walkable if it does not contain any kind considered impassable\n    for k in impassable_kinds:\n      if grid[r, c, k] > 0:\n        return False\n    return True\n\n  # 2. Locate `primitive` on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for r in range(height):\n    for c in range(width):\n      if grid[r, c, primitive] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    # Primitive not found on the grid, cannot collect\n    return []\n\n  # 3. BFS to find the shortest path from current_pos to a cell adjacent to any primitive\n  # `q` stores (r, c) for BFS traversal\n  # `parent_map` stores (r, c) -> (prev_r, prev_c, action_to_reach_current) for path reconstruction\n  q = collections.deque([(current_pos[0], current_pos[1])])\n  visited = {(current_pos[0], current_pos[1])}\n  parent_map = {} # (child_r, child_c) -> (parent_r, parent_c, action_from_parent)\n\n  target_adj_pos = None # The best adjacent cell to a primitive we want to reach\n  actual_primitive_pos = None # The specific primitive location adjacent to target_adj_pos\n\n  while q:\n    r, c = q.popleft()\n\n    # Check if this cell (r, c) is already adjacent to a primitive\n    # This ensures we prioritize paths that lead directly to an adjacent spot\n    for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n      if abs(r - pr) + abs(c - pc) == 1: # Manhattan distance of 1 means adjacent\n        target_adj_pos = (r, c)\n        actual_primitive_pos = (pr, pc)\n        q.clear() # Found target, stop BFS\n        break\n    \n    if target_adj_pos:\n      break # Exit outer loop if target found\n\n    # Explore neighbors\n    for action, (dr, dc) in _ACTION_TO_DELTA.items():\n      nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n\n      if (nr, nc) in visited:\n        continue\n\n      if is_walkable(nr, nc):\n        visited.add((nr, nc))\n        parent_map[(nr, nc)] = (r, c, action)\n        q.append((nr, nc))\n\n  if target_adj_pos is None:\n    # No path found to any cell adjacent to a primitive\n    return []\n\n  # 4. Reconstruct path from current_pos to target_adj_pos\n  path_to_target_adj = []\n  curr = target_adj_pos\n  while curr != current_pos:\n    prev_r, prev_c, action_from_prev = parent_map[curr]\n    path_to_target_adj.append(action_from_prev)\n    curr = (prev_r, prev_c)\n  \n  all_actions = path_to_target_adj[::-1] # Reverse to get actions in correct order\n\n  # 5. Determine desired direction to face the primitive after reaching target_adj_pos\n  # Calculate relative position of primitive from target_adj_pos\n  dr_to_prim = actual_primitive_pos[0] - target_adj_pos[0]\n  dc_to_prim = actual_primitive_pos[1] - target_adj_pos[1]\n\n  desired_dir = -1\n  if dr_to_prim == -1: # Primitive is North of agent\n      desired_dir = NORTH\n  elif dr_to_prim == 1: # Primitive is South of agent\n      desired_dir = SOUTH\n  elif dc_to_prim == -1: # Primitive is West of agent\n      desired_dir = WEST\n  elif dc_to_prim == 1: # Primitive is East of agent\n      desired_dir = EAST\n  \n  if desired_dir == -1: # Should not happen if primitive is truly adjacent\n      return [] # Error or invalid state\n\n  # 6. Add turning actions to face the primitive\n  # The agent's direction is assumed to remain `initial_dir` after only movement actions.\n  turn_actions = _TURN_ACTIONS_MAP.get((initial_dir, desired_dir))\n  if turn_actions is None:\n      # This indicates an issue with the direction mapping\n      return []\n\n  all_actions.extend(turn_actions)\n  \n  # 7. Add `USE` action to collect the primitive\n  all_actions.append(USE)\n\n  return all_actions", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:53:18.173700", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:53:19.166457", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  DOWN_ACTION = 0\n  UP_ACTION = 1\n  LEFT_ACTION = 2\n  RIGHT_ACTION = 3\n  USE_ACTION = 4\n\n  NORTH_DIR = 0\n  EAST_DIR = 1\n  SOUTH_DIR = 2\n  WEST_DIR = 3\n\n  # Helper function: Calculates direction agent needs to face to look at an item\n  def _get_target_facing_direction(agent_x, agent_y, item_x, item_y):\n    dx = item_x - agent_x\n    dy = item_y - agent_y\n\n    if dx == 0 and dy == 0:\n      return None\n\n    # Determine primary axis movement (horizontal or vertical) for facing\n    if abs(dx) >= abs(dy): # Prioritize horizontal if magnitude is greater or equal\n      return EAST_DIR if dx > 0 else WEST_DIR\n    else: # abs(dy) > abs(dx)\n      return SOUTH_DIR if dy > 0 else NORTH_DIR\n\n  # Helper function: Returns actions to turn from current_dir to target_dir.\n  # Assumes LEFT_ACTION and RIGHT_ACTION are used for turning.\n  def _get_turn_actions(current_dir, target_dir):\n    actions = []\n    if current_dir == target_dir:\n      return []\n\n    clockwise_turns = (target_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n    counter_clockwise_turns = (current_dir - target_dir + 4) % 4\n\n    if clockwise_turns <= counter_clockwise_turns:\n      for _ in range(clockwise_turns):\n        actions.append(RIGHT_ACTION) # Turn right\n    else:\n      for _ in range(counter_clockwise_turns):\n        actions.append(LEFT_ACTION) # Turn left\n    return actions\n\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  agent_grid = current_state.grid\n  agent_pos_x, agent_pos_y = current_state.pos\n  agent_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction\n\n  grid_height, grid_width, _ = agent_grid.shape\n\n  # Find all locations of the primitive on the grid\n  y_coords, x_coords = np.where(agent_grid[:, :, primitive_id] == 1)\n\n  if len(x_coords) == 0:\n    return [] # Primitive not found on the grid\n\n  # Step 1: Identify all potential collection points.\n  # These are cells from which the agent can be adjacent to *any* instance of the primitive\n  # and perform a USE action.\n  primitive_locations = set()\n  for i in range(len(x_coords)):\n    primitive_locations.add((x_coords[i], y_coords[i]))\n  \n  potential_collection_points = set()\n  # Define deltas for checking cardinal adjacency\n  ADJACENCY_DELTAS = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)] \n\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    for dx, dy in ADJACENCY_DELTAS:\n      adj_x, adj_y = px + dx, py + dy\n      if 0 <= adj_x < grid_width and 0 <= adj_y < grid_height:\n        # A cell is a potential collection point if it's within bounds AND\n        # 1. It's not occupied by the primitive itself (agent cannot move onto the item it wants to collect).\n        if agent_grid[adj_y, adj_x, primitive_id] == 1:\n            continue\n        \n        # 2. It's not occupied by any non-grabbable obstacle (e.g., water, lava, walls).\n        # Assuming non_grabbable_indices are impassable for agent movement.\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        for obstacle_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n            if agent_grid[adj_y, adj_x, obstacle_idx] == 1:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n                break\n        \n        if not is_impassable_obstacle:\n            potential_collection_points.add((adj_x, adj_y))\n  \n  if not potential_collection_points:\n      return [] # No valid collection points (e.g., item might be completely surrounded by other items or walls)\n\n  # Step 2: BFS Pathfinding to *any* of the potential_collection_points.\n  # The BFS finds the shortest path.\n  queue = [(agent_pos_x, agent_pos_y, [])]\n  visited = set([(agent_pos_x, agent_pos_y)])\n  \n  path_to_adj_pos = []\n  chosen_adj_pos = None # The specific adjacent position the agent will move to\n  target_item_pos_for_facing = None # The specific primitive instance to face\n\n  # Define movement deltas for BFS. These actions move the agent cardinally.\n  # They do NOT change the agent's facing direction.\n  ACTION_MOVES = {\n      UP_ACTION: (0, -1),\n      DOWN_ACTION: (0, 1),\n      LEFT_ACTION: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT_ACTION: (1, 0),\n  }\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_x, curr_y, current_path = queue.pop(0)\n\n    # Check if the current position is one of the potential collection points\n    if (curr_x, curr_y) in potential_collection_points:\n      path_to_adj_pos = current_path\n      chosen_adj_pos = (curr_x, curr_y)\n      \n      # Now, identify *which* primitive instance this chosen_adj_pos is adjacent to.\n      # Any adjacent primitive will do for the USE action, so pick the first one found.\n      for dx, dy in ADJACENCY_DELTAS:\n          item_x, item_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n          if 0 <= item_x < grid_width and 0 <= item_y < grid_height and\\\n             agent_grid[item_y, item_x, primitive_id] == 1: # Check if this specific primitive instance is there\n              target_item_pos_for_facing = (item_x, item_y)\n              break # Found the target item for facing\n      break # Path found to a valid collection point, exit BFS\n\n    # Explore possible moves from current position\n    for action, (dx, dy) in ACTION_MOVES.items():\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n\n      # Check boundary conditions and if the cell has not been visited yet\n      if 0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height and\\\n         (next_x, next_y) not in visited:\n        \n        # Ensure the next cell is traversable for movement.\n        # 1. Cannot move onto the primitive itself\n        if agent_grid[next_y, next_x, primitive_id] == 1:\n            continue # This cell contains the primitive, cannot move onto it\n\n        # 2. Cannot move onto any non-grabbable obstacle (e.g., water, lava, walls)\n        is_impassable_obstacle = False\n        for obstacle_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n            if agent_grid[next_y, next_x, obstacle_idx] == 1:\n                is_impassable_obstacle = True\n                break\n        \n        if is_impassable_obstacle:\n            continue # This cell contains an impassable obstacle, cannot move onto it\n\n        # If it passes all checks, it's traversable\n        visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n        queue.append((next_x, next_y, current_path + [action]))\n\n  # If no path was found to any collection point (queue exhausted before finding a target)\n  if chosen_adj_pos is None:\n    return []\n\n  final_actions = list(path_to_adj_pos)\n\n  # After moving to the chosen_adj_pos, determine the direction the agent needs to face\n  # the primitive and add the necessary turning actions.\n  # The agent's `dir` (initial direction) is used as `current_dir` because the movement actions\n  # (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) do not change the agent's facing direction.\n  if target_item_pos_for_facing is not None:\n    target_face_dir = _get_target_facing_direction(chosen_adj_pos[0], chosen_adj_pos[1], \n                                                   target_item_pos_for_facing[0], target_item_pos_for_facing[1])\n    if target_face_dir is not None:\n      final_actions.extend(_get_turn_actions(agent_dir, target_face_dir))\n  \n  # Finally, add the USE action to collect the primitive\n  final_actions.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return final_actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:54:59.875143", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import heapq\n\n  # Action and Direction Constants\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  DIR_UP = 0\n  DIR_RIGHT = 1\n  DIR_DOWN = 2\n  DIR_LEFT = 3\n\n  DIR_DELTAS = {\n      DIR_UP: (0, -1),   # Moving up: x constant, y decreases\n      DIR_RIGHT: (1, 0),  # Moving right: x increases, y constant\n      DIR_DOWN: (0, 1),   # Moving down: x constant, y increases\n      DIR_LEFT: (-1, 0),  # Moving left: x decreases, y constant\n  }\n\n  # Pre-compute a reverse mapping for faster lookup of required agent direction.\n  VECTOR_TO_DIR = {v: k for k, v in DIR_DELTAS.items()}\n\n  ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR = {\n      ACTION_UP: DIR_UP,\n      ACTION_RIGHT: DIR_RIGHT,\n      ACTION_DOWN: DIR_DOWN,\n      ACTION_LEFT: DIR_LEFT,\n  }\n\n  MOVEMENT_ACTIONS = [ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT]\n\n  def _heuristic(state, primitive_locs):\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the Manhattan distance heuristic for A* search.\n      This estimates the minimum number of moves from the current agent state (position)\n      to any of the primitive locations. It is admissible (never overestimates).\n      \"\"\"\n      s_x, s_y, _ = state\n      if not primitive_locs:\n          return 0\n      min_dist = float('inf')\n      for p_x, p_y in primitive_locs:\n          min_dist = min(min_dist, abs(s_x - p_x) + abs(s_y - p_y))\n      return min_dist\n\n  # 1. Get current state information from the environment.\n  obs = env.observations()\n  grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n  \n  # Extract current agent position (x, y) and direction.\n  # Note: pos is normalized, convert to int grid coordinates.\n  current_pos_x, current_pos_y = obs['features_dict']['pos'].astype(int)\n  current_dir = np.argmax(obs['features_dict']['direction'])\n\n  # Get world configuration, specifically non-grabbable entities that act as obstacles.\n  world = env.world\n  non_grabbable_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 2. Determine traversable cells on the grid.\n  # A cell is considered NOT traversable if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n  traversable_mask = np.ones((grid_width, grid_height), dtype=bool)\n  if non_grabbable_indices:\n      # Use np.any along the kind-axis to find if any non-grabbable item is present.\n      # Convert set to list for NumPy advanced indexing.\n      cells_with_obstacles = np.any(grid[:, :, list(non_grabbable_indices)] > 0, axis=2)\n      traversable_mask[cells_with_obstacles] = False\n  \n  # The agent's starting position must be traversable to begin the search.\n  if not traversable_mask[current_pos_x, current_pos_y]:\n      return [] # Cannot start from an untraversable point.\n\n  # 3. Identify all locations on the grid where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = []\n  # np.where returns (row_indices, col_indices). For grid[x, y, kind], x is column, y is row.\n  # So, for grid[:, :, primitive], the first array from np.where is y-coordinates, second is x-coordinates.\n  y_coords_of_primitive, x_coords_of_primitive = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive] > 0)\n  for x, y in zip(x_coords_of_primitive, y_coords_of_primitive):\n      primitive_locations_on_grid.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      return [] # The primitive is not present anywhere on the map.\n\n  # 4. Identify \"collectable target states\" for the agent.\n  # A target state is (agent_x, agent_y, agent_direction) from which the ACTION_USE\n  # can successfully collect the primitive. This requires the agent to be adjacent\n  # to the primitive and facing it.\n  collectable_target_states = set()\n  for p_x, p_y in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      # Iterate over the four cells adjacent to the primitive.\n      for delta_x_from_primitive, delta_y_from_primitive in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n          # Calculate the agent's potential position (a_x, a_y) if it were to face the primitive.\n          a_x, a_y = p_x + delta_x_from_primitive, p_y + delta_y_from_primitive\n\n          # Check if this potential agent position is within grid boundaries and is traversable.\n          if not (0 <= a_x < grid_width and 0 <= a_y < grid_height and traversable_mask[a_x, a_y]):\n              continue\n          \n          # Determine the required direction the agent must face from (a_x, a_y) to collect (p_x, p_y).\n          # This vector goes from agent's position to primitive's position.\n          vector_to_primitive_x, vector_to_primitive_y = p_x - a_x, p_y - a_y\n\n          # Use the pre-computed VECTOR_TO_DIR map for a more direct and efficient lookup.\n          required_agent_dir = VECTOR_TO_DIR.get((vector_to_primitive_x, vector_to_primitive_y), -1)\n          \n          if required_agent_dir != -1: # Ensure a valid direction was found.\n              collectable_target_states.add((a_x, a_y, required_agent_dir))\n\n  if not collectable_target_states:\n      return [] # No valid states exist from which the primitive can be collected.\n\n  # 5. Perform A* Search on the state space.\n  # A state is defined by (agent_x, agent_y, agent_direction).\n  start_state = (current_pos_x, current_pos_y, current_dir)\n  \n  # g_score: actual cost from start_state to current state\n  # Initialized with infinity for all states except start_state\n  g_score = {start_state: 0}\n  \n  # priority_queue: stores (f_score, state_tuple)\n  # f_score = g_score + h_score (heuristic estimate from state to goal)\n  # The first element in the tuple determines priority (min-heap)\n  priority_queue = [(0 + _heuristic(start_state, primitive_locations_on_grid), start_state)]\n  \n  # came_from: maps a state to the (previous_state, action_taken_to_reach_current_state)\n  # Used to reconstruct the path after finding the goal.\n  came_from = {}\n\n  while priority_queue:\n      # Get the state with the lowest f_score from the priority queue.\n      current_f_score, current_state = heapq.heappop(priority_queue)\n      curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir = current_state\n\n      # Check if this entry from the priority queue is stale.\n      # A stale entry means a shorter path to `current_state` has already been found\n      # and processed (i.e., `g_score[current_state]` is better than the G-score corresponding\n      # to `current_f_score` popped from heap).\n      if current_f_score > g_score.get(current_state, float('inf')) + _heuristic(current_state, primitive_locations_on_grid):\n           continue # Skip this outdated entry.\n        \n      # Check if the current state is one of our desired collectable target states.\n      if current_state in collectable_target_states:\n          # If it is, we've found the shortest path. Reconstruct and return.\n          path = []\n          temp_state = current_state\n          while temp_state != start_state:\n              prev_state, action = came_from[temp_state]\n              path.append(action)\n              temp_state = prev_state\n          \n          # The path is built in reverse order, so reverse it and append the ACTION_USE.\n          return path[::-1] + [ACTION_USE]\n\n      # Explore all possible next states by applying movement actions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n      for action_taken in MOVEMENT_ACTIONS:\n          # Determine the agent's new direction and position after taking this action.\n          next_dir = ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR[action_taken]\n          dx_move, dy_move = DIR_DELTAS[next_dir]\n          \n          next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx_move, curr_y + dy_move\n          next_state = (next_x, next_y, next_dir)\n\n          # Check if the next cell is within grid boundaries and is traversable.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height and traversable_mask[next_x, next_y]):\n              continue # Invalid or blocked move.\n          \n          # Calculate the cost to reach this next_state from the start state via the current_state.\n          # Each movement action costs 1.\n          tentative_g_score = g_score[current_state] + 1 \n\n          # If this new path to `next_state` is shorter than any previously found path,\n          # or if `next_state` hasn't been reached yet, update its score and add to queue.\n          if tentative_g_score < g_score.get(next_state, float('inf')):\n              came_from[next_state] = (current_state, action_taken)\n              g_score[next_state] = tentative_g_score\n              \n              # Calculate the f_score for the `next_state` and push it to the priority queue.\n              f_score_next = tentative_g_score + _heuristic(next_state, primitive_locations_on_grid)\n              heapq.heappush(priority_queue, (f_score_next, next_state))\n  \n  # If the priority queue becomes empty and no path to a target state was found, return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:55:00.869364", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import heapq # This import must be inside the function if it's not global\n                # to adhere to the instruction \"Please only return code that will fit in that function. Do not imports or add the function signature on the top.\"\n\n  # --- Constants for CraftWorld Actions and Directions ---\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  DIR_UP = 0\n  DIR_RIGHT = 1\n  DIR_DOWN = 2\n  DIR_LEFT = 3\n\n  DIR_DELTAS = {\n      DIR_UP: (0, -1),   # (dx, dy) for moving UP (y decreases)\n      DIR_RIGHT: (1, 0),  # (dx, dy) for moving RIGHT (x increases)\n      DIR_DOWN: (0, 1),   # (dx, dy) for moving DOWN (y increases)\n      DIR_LEFT: (-1, 0),  # (dx, dy) for moving LEFT (x decreases)\n  }\n\n  # Maps a (dx, dy) vector to the corresponding agent direction enum.\n  VECTOR_TO_DIR = {v: k for k, v in DIR_DELTAS.items()}\n\n  # Maps a movement action to the resulting agent direction.\n  ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR = {\n      ACTION_UP: DIR_UP,\n      ACTION_RIGHT: DIR_RIGHT,\n      ACTION_DOWN: DIR_DOWN,\n      ACTION_LEFT: DIR_LEFT,\n  }\n\n  MOVEMENT_ACTIONS = [ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT]\n  # --- End Constants ---\n\n  # Helper for heuristic (Manhattan distance to closest primitive location)\n  def _heuristic(state, primitive_locs):\n      \"\"\"Calculates the Manhattan distance heuristic from the current state to the closest primitive location.\"\"\"\n      s_x, s_y, _ = state\n      if not primitive_locs:\n          return 0\n      min_dist = float('inf')\n      for p_x, p_y in primitive_locs:\n          min_dist = min(min_dist, abs(s_x - p_x) + abs(s_y - p_y))\n      return min_dist\n\n  # 1. Get current state information from the environment.\n  obs = env.observations()\n  grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n\n  # Extract current agent position (x, y) and direction.\n  current_pos_x, current_pos_y = obs['features_dict']['pos'].astype(int)\n  current_dir = np.argmax(obs['features_dict']['direction'])\n\n  # Get world configuration, specifically non-grabbable entities that act as obstacles.\n  world = env.world\n  non_grabbable_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 2. Determine traversable cells on the grid.\n  # A cell is considered NOT traversable if it contains any non-grabbable item.\n  traversable_mask = np.ones((grid_width, grid_height), dtype=bool)\n  if non_grabbable_indices:\n      # Create a boolean mask where True indicates an obstacle of any non-grabbable kind.\n      cells_with_obstacles = np.any(grid[:, :, list(non_grabbable_indices)] > 0, axis=2)\n      traversable_mask[cells_with_obstacles] = False\n\n  # The agent's starting position must be traversable to begin the search.\n  if not traversable_mask[current_pos_x, current_pos_y]:\n      return [] # Cannot move from an untraversable starting point.\n\n  # 3. Identify all locations on the grid where the target primitive exists.\n  primitive_locations_on_grid = []\n  # np.where returns (row_indices, col_indices) which correspond to (y, x)\n  y_coords_of_primitive, x_coords_of_primitive = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive] > 0)\n  for x, y in zip(x_coords_of_primitive, y_coords_of_primitive):\n      primitive_locations_on_grid.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      return [] # The primitive is not present anywhere on the map.\n\n  # 4. Identify \"collectable target states\" for the agent.\n  # A target state is (agent_x, agent_y, agent_direction) from which the ACTION_USE\n  # can successfully collect the primitive. This requires the agent to be adjacent\n  # to the primitive and facing it.\n  collectable_target_states = set()\n  for p_x, p_y in primitive_locations_on_grid:\n      # Iterate over the four cells adjacent to the primitive.\n      for delta_x_from_primitive, delta_y_from_primitive in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n          # Calculate the agent's potential position (a_x, a_y).\n          a_x, a_y = p_x + delta_x_from_primitive, p_y + delta_y_from_primitive\n\n          # Check if this potential agent position is within grid boundaries and is traversable.\n          if not (0 <= a_x < grid_width and 0 <= a_y < grid_height and traversable_mask[a_x, a_y]):\n              continue\n\n          # Determine the required direction the agent must face from (a_x, a_y) to collect (p_x, p_y).\n          vector_to_primitive_x, vector_to_primitive_y = p_x - a_x, p_y - a_y\n\n          # Use the pre-computed VECTOR_TO_DIR map for a more direct lookup.\n          required_agent_dir = VECTOR_TO_DIR.get((vector_to_primitive_x, vector_to_primitive_y), -1)\n\n          if required_agent_dir != -1:\n              collectable_target_states.add((a_x, a_y, required_agent_dir))\n\n  if not collectable_target_states:\n      return [] # No valid states exist from which the primitive can be collected.\n\n  # 5. Perform A* Search on the state space.\n  # A state is defined by (agent_x, agent_y, agent_direction).\n  start_state = (current_pos_x, current_pos_y, current_dir)\n\n  # g_score: actual cost from start_state to current state\n  # Initialized with infinity for all states except start_state\n  g_score = {start_state: 0}\n\n  # priority_queue: stores (f_score, state_tuple)\n  # f_score = g_score + h_score (heuristic estimate from state to goal)\n  # The first element in the tuple determines priority (min-heap)\n  priority_queue = [(0 + _heuristic(start_state, primitive_locations_on_grid), start_state)]\n\n  # came_from: maps a state to the (previous_state, action_taken_to_reach_current_state)\n  # Used to reconstruct the path after finding the goal.\n  came_from = {}\n\n  while priority_queue:\n      # Get the state with the lowest f_score from the priority queue.\n      current_f_score, current_state = heapq.heappop(priority_queue)\n      curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir = current_state\n\n      # If we extracted a state with a higher f_score than what's currently recorded\n      # in g_score (meaning a shorter path to this state has already been found and processed),\n      # then skip this outdated entry. This handles cases where a state is added to the\n      # priority queue multiple times with different paths, and we only want to process\n      # the shortest one.\n      if current_f_score > g_score.get(current_state, float('inf')) + _heuristic(current_state, primitive_locations_on_grid):\n           continue\n\n      # Check if the current state is one of our desired collectable target states.\n      if current_state in collectable_target_states:\n          # If it is, we've found the shortest path. Reconstruct and return.\n          path = []\n          temp_state = current_state\n          while temp_state != start_state:\n              prev_state, action = came_from[temp_state]\n              path.append(action)\n              temp_state = prev_state\n\n          # The path is built in reverse, so reverse it and append the ACTION_USE.\n          return path[::-1] + [ACTION_USE]\n\n      # Explore all possible next states by applying movement actions.\n      for action_taken in MOVEMENT_ACTIONS:\n          # Determine the agent's new direction and position after taking this action.\n          next_dir = ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR[action_taken]\n          dx_move, dy_move = DIR_DELTAS[next_dir]\n\n          next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx_move, curr_y + dy_move\n          next_state = (next_x, next_y, next_dir)\n\n          # Check if the next cell is within grid boundaries and is traversable.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < grid_width and 0 <= next_y < grid_height and traversable_mask[next_x, next_y]):\n              continue\n\n          # Calculate the cost to reach this next_state from the start state via the current_state.\n          # Each movement action costs 1.\n          tentative_g_score = g_score[current_state] + 1\n\n          # If this new path to next_state is shorter than any previously found path,\n          # or if next_state hasn't been reached yet, update its score and add to queue.\n          if tentative_g_score < g_score.get(next_state, float('inf')):\n              came_from[next_state] = (current_state, action_taken)\n              g_score[next_state] = tentative_g_score\n\n              # Calculate the f_score for the next_state and push to the priority queue.\n              f_score_next = tentative_g_score + _heuristic(next_state, primitive_locations_on_grid)\n              heapq.heappush(priority_queue, (f_score_next, next_state))\n\n  # If the priority queue becomes empty and no path to a target state was found, return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:56:48.259669", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Define direction constants for agent's orientation (internal representation)\n  _DIR_UP = 0\n  _DIR_RIGHT = 1\n  _DIR_DOWN = 2\n  _DIR_LEFT = 3\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment\n  _actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  _DOWN = _actions_map['DOWN']\n  _UP = _actions_map['UP']\n  _LEFT = _actions_map['LEFT']\n  _RIGHT = _actions_map['RIGHT']\n  _USE = _actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Get current state information from the environment's observations\n  obs = env.observations()\n  features_dict = obs['features_dict']\n  \n  current_grid = features_dict['features_global'] # Full allocentric grid\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions from the scenario\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = env.scenario.init_grid.shape\n\n  # Denormalize current agent position (features_dict['pos'] is normalized 0-1)\n  current_pos_normalized = features_dict['pos']\n  current_px = int(round(current_pos_normalized[0] * (WIDTH - 1)))\n  current_py = int(round(current_pos_normalized[1] * (HEIGHT - 1)))\n  \n  # Get current agent direction (convert one-hot array to integer 0-3)\n  current_dir_int = np.argmax(features_dict['direction'])\n\n  # Early exit if the primitive is not grabbable, as it cannot be collected\n  if primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Find all grid locations where the primitive exists\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(WIDTH):\n    for y in range(HEIGHT):\n      if current_grid[x, y, primitive] == 1: \n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no primitive is found on the grid, return an empty list of actions\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # Define truly impassable terrain indices for agent movement.\n  # Assuming 'water' is the primary obstacle. Other non-grabbable items like workshops\n  # are typically traversable, but not grabbable.\n  impassable_for_movement = {env.world.water_index} \n\n  def is_obstacle(x, y, grid, impassable_kinds_set, target_primitive_idx):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the cell (x,y) contains any truly impassable item for agent movement.\n    The target_primitive_idx is explicitly *not* considered an obstacle for movement,\n    as the goal is to interact with it.\n    \"\"\"\n    for k in impassable_kinds_set:\n      if k == target_primitive_idx:\n          continue # Do not block movement if the obstacle is the target primitive itself.\n      \n      if grid[x, y, k] == 1: \n        return True # Found an impassable kind that is not our target\n    return False\n\n  # Pre-calculate all target interaction states for all primitive locations.\n  # An interaction state is (adjacent_x, adjacent_y, required_facing_direction)\n  # from which the agent can successfully _USE_ the primitive.\n  target_interaction_states = set()\n  for Px, Py in primitive_locations:\n      # Agent needs to be at an adjacent cell and face the primitive\n      if Px - 1 >= 0:  target_interaction_states.add((Px - 1, Py, _DIR_RIGHT))\n      if Px + 1 < WIDTH: target_interaction_states.add((Px + 1, Py, _DIR_LEFT))\n      if Py - 1 >= 0:  target_interaction_states.add((Px, Py - 1, _DIR_DOWN))\n      if Py + 1 < HEIGHT: target_interaction_states.add((Px, Py + 1, _DIR_UP))\n    \n  # Helper for calculating minimum turns needed to change direction\n  def min_turns(current_dir, target_dir):\n      diff = abs(current_dir - target_dir)\n      return min(diff, 4 - diff)\n\n  # Admissible heuristic function for A* (estimated cost from current state to nearest goal)\n  # Uses Manhattan distance to the closest (x,y) location of any target interaction point.\n  # Direction is not directly included as movement actions change orientation.\n  def heuristic(cx, cy, c_dir): # c_dir is unused for this heuristic\n      min_h = float('inf')\n      for tx, ty, _ in target_interaction_states:\n          min_h = min(min_h, abs(cx - tx) + abs(cy - ty)) # Manhattan distance\n      return min_h\n\n  # A* search setup\n  # Priority queue stores tuples: (f_score, g_score, (x, y, dir), path_actions)\n  # f_score = g_score + h_score\n  pq = []\n  \n  start_state = (current_px, current_py, current_dir_int)\n  \n  start_g_score = 0\n  start_h_score = heuristic(current_px, current_py, current_dir_int)\n  start_f_score = start_g_score + start_h_score\n\n  heapq.heappush(pq, (start_f_score, start_g_score, start_state, [])) \n  \n  # Dictionary to store the minimum g_score found so far for each state (x, y, dir)\n  g_scores = {start_state: 0} \n\n  # Define possible movement actions and their resulting new position/direction\n  # (dx, dy, environment_action_id, new_agent_direction_constant)\n  move_actions_info = [\n      (0, -1, _UP, _DIR_UP),    # Move up, agent faces up\n      (0, 1, _DOWN, _DIR_DOWN),  # Move down, agent faces down\n      (-1, 0, _LEFT, _DIR_LEFT), # Move left, agent faces left\n      (1, 0, _RIGHT, _DIR_RIGHT) # Move right, agent faces right\n  ]\n\n  # Define turning actions (in-place rotation)\n  # (environment_action_id, direction_offset)\n  turn_actions_info = [\n      (_LEFT, -1), # Turn left (counter-clockwise)\n      (_RIGHT, 1)  # Turn right (clockwise)\n  ]\n\n  # Main A* loop\n  while pq:\n    f_score, g_score, (cx, cy, c_dir), current_path = heapq.heappop(pq)\n\n    # If we found a shorter path to this state already, skip this one\n    if g_score > g_scores.get((cx, cy, c_dir), float('inf')):\n        continue\n\n    # Check if the current state is one of the goal interaction states\n    if (cx, cy, c_dir) in target_interaction_states:\n        # Goal reached: agent is at a valid adjacent position, facing the primitive.\n        # Append the _USE action as the final step and return the path.\n        return current_path + [_USE]\n\n    # Explore movement actions\n    for dx, dy, move_action_id, n_dir_after_move in move_actions_info:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n\n      # Check for valid grid bounds and if the new cell is an obstacle\n      if not (0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT):\n        continue # Out of bounds\n      if is_obstacle(nx, ny, current_grid, impassable_for_movement, primitive):\n        continue # Obstacle present\n\n      new_state = (nx, ny, n_dir_after_move) \n      new_g_score = g_score + 1 # Each move action costs 1\n\n      if new_g_score < g_scores.get(new_state, float('inf')):\n        g_scores[new_state] = new_g_score\n        new_h_score = heuristic(nx, ny, n_dir_after_move)\n        new_f_score = new_g_score + new_h_score\n        heapq.heappush(pq, (new_f_score, new_g_score, new_state, current_path + [move_action_id]))\n\n    # Explore turning actions (agent stays in the same cell but changes direction)\n    for turn_action_id, dir_offset in turn_actions_info:\n        n_dir_after_turn = (c_dir + dir_offset + 4) % 4 # Ensure direction wraps correctly (0-3)\n        new_state = (cx, cy, n_dir_after_turn)\n        new_g_score = g_score + 1 # Each turn action costs 1\n\n        if new_g_score < g_scores.get(new_state, float('inf')):\n            g_scores[new_state] = new_g_score\n            new_h_score = heuristic(cx, cy, n_dir_after_turn)\n            new_f_score = new_g_score + new_h_score\n            heapq.heappush(pq, (new_f_score, new_g_score, new_state, current_path + [turn_action_id]))\n\n  # If A* finishes and no path was found (e.g., primitive is entirely unreachable)\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:56:49.313531", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Define direction constants for agent's orientation (internal representation)\n  # These map to the integer values of the one-hot direction encoding in features_dict['direction']\n  _DIR_UP = 0\n  _DIR_RIGHT = 1\n  _DIR_DOWN = 2\n  _DIR_LEFT = 3\n\n  # Get action mappings from the environment for cleaner code\n  _actions_map = env.action_specs()\n  _DOWN = _actions_map['DOWN']\n  _UP = _actions_map['UP']\n  _LEFT = _actions_map['LEFT']\n  _RIGHT = _actions_map['RIGHT']\n  _USE = _actions_map['USE']\n\n  # Get current state information from the environment's observations\n  obs = env.observations()\n  features_dict = obs['features_dict']\n  \n  current_grid = features_dict['features_global'] # Full allocentric grid copy\n  \n  # Get grid dimensions from the scenario (assuming they are consistent throughout an episode)\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = env.scenario.init_grid.shape\n\n  # Denormalize current agent position. features_dict['pos'] is normalized (0-1).\n  current_pos_normalized = features_dict['pos']\n  current_px = int(round(current_pos_normalized[0] * (WIDTH - 1)))\n  current_py = int(round(current_pos_normalized[1] * (HEIGHT - 1)))\n  \n  # Get current agent direction from its one-hot encoding\n  current_dir_int = np.argmax(features_dict['direction'])\n\n  # Early exit if the primitive cannot be collected (e.g., it's a non-grabbable environment item)\n  if primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Find all grid locations where the primitive exists\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for x in range(WIDTH):\n    for y in range(HEIGHT):\n      # Assuming current_grid[x, y, kind_index] == 1 indicates presence of that kind\n      if current_grid[x, y, primitive] == 1: \n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  # If no primitive is found on the grid, return an empty list of actions\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    return []\n\n  # Define impassable terrain for agent movement.\n  # Water is typically impassable. Workshops are usually fixed structures that block movement.\n  impassable_movement_terrain_indices = {env.world.water_index}\n  if env.world.workshop_indices: # Ensure the list is not empty before adding\n      impassable_movement_terrain_indices.update(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n  def is_obstacle(x, y, grid, impassable_kinds_set):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the cell (x,y) contains any entity that blocks agent movement.\n    Assumes (x,y) is within grid bounds.\n    \"\"\"\n    for k in impassable_kinds_set:\n      if grid[x, y, k] == 1: \n        return True\n    return False\n\n  # --- BFS for shortest path to an *interaction point* ---\n  # The agent needs to be adjacent to the primitive and facing it to _USE_ it.\n  # BFS queue stores tuples: ((current_x, current_y, current_direction), [path_actions_taken])\n  q = collections.deque()\n  start_state = (current_px, current_py, current_dir_int)\n  q.append((start_state, [])) \n  \n  # Set to store visited states (position + direction) to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n  visited = {start_state} \n\n  # Define possible movement actions and their resulting new position and agent direction.\n  # Format: (dx, dy, environment_action_id, new_agent_direction_constant)\n  move_actions_info = [\n      (0, -1, _UP, _DIR_UP),    # Move up (Y-1), agent faces up\n      (0, 1, _DOWN, _DIR_DOWN),  # Move down (Y+1), agent faces down\n      (-1, 0, _LEFT, _DIR_LEFT), # Move left (X-1), agent faces left\n      (1, 0, _RIGHT, _DIR_RIGHT) # Move right (X+1), agent faces right\n  ]\n\n  # Define turning actions (in-place rotation)\n  # Format: (environment_action_id, direction_offset)\n  # Offset: -1 for left turn (counter-clockwise), +1 for right turn (clockwise)\n  turn_actions_info = [\n      (_LEFT, -1), \n      (_RIGHT, 1)  \n  ]\n\n  # Pre-calculate all target interaction states for all primitive locations.\n  # A target interaction state is (adjacent_x, adjacent_y, required_facing_direction)\n  # from which the agent can successfully _USE_ the primitive at (Px, Py).\n  target_interaction_states = set()\n  for Px, Py in primitive_locations:\n      # If agent is at (Px-1, Py), it needs to face RIGHT (_DIR_RIGHT) to use (Px, Py)\n      if Px - 1 >= 0:  target_interaction_states.add((Px - 1, Py, _DIR_RIGHT))\n      # If agent is at (Px+1, Py), it needs to face LEFT (_DIR_LEFT) to use (Px, Py)\n      if Px + 1 < WIDTH: target_interaction_states.add((Px + 1, Py, _DIR_LEFT))\n      # If agent is at (Px, Py-1), it needs to face DOWN (_DIR_DOWN) to use (Px, Py)\n      if Py - 1 >= 0:  target_interaction_states.add((Px, Py - 1, _DIR_DOWN))\n      # If agent is at (Px, Py+1), it needs to face UP (_DIR_UP) to use (Px, Py)\n      if Py + 1 < HEIGHT: target_interaction_states.add((Px, Py + 1, _DIR_UP))\n    \n  # Main BFS loop\n  while q:\n    (cx, cy, c_dir), current_path = q.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current state is one of the goal interaction states.\n    # If so, the agent is positioned correctly and facing the primitive.\n    if (cx, cy, c_dir) in target_interaction_states:\n        # Goal reached: agent is at a valid adjacent position, facing the primitive.\n        # Append the _USE action as the final step and return the path.\n        # BFS guarantees this is the shortest path in terms of action count.\n        return current_path + [_USE]\n\n    # Explore movement actions (move to an adjacent cell)\n    for dx, dy, move_action_id, n_dir_after_move in move_actions_info:\n      nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n\n      # Check for valid grid bounds and if the new cell is an obstacle\n      if not (0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT):\n        continue # Out of bounds\n      if is_obstacle(nx, ny, current_grid, impassable_movement_terrain_indices):\n        continue # Obstacle present at the target cell\n\n      new_state = (nx, ny, n_dir_after_move) \n      if new_state not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_state)\n        q.append((new_state, current_path + [move_action_id]))\n\n    # Explore turning actions (agent stays in the same cell but changes direction)\n    for turn_action_id, dir_offset in turn_actions_info:\n        # Calculate new direction, ensuring it wraps around correctly (0-3)\n        n_dir_after_turn = (c_dir + dir_offset + 4) % 4 \n        new_state = (cx, cy, n_dir_after_turn)\n        if new_state not in visited:\n            visited.add(new_state)\n            q.append((new_state, current_path + [turn_action_id]))\n\n  # If BFS finishes and no path was found (e.g., the primitive is entirely unreachable\n  # due to impassable terrain or being surrounded by other primitives already in inventory),\n  # return an empty list of actions.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:58:06.681954", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T18:58:07.671376", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  DOWN_ACTION = 0\n  UP_ACTION = 1\n  LEFT_ACTION = 2\n  RIGHT_ACTION = 3\n  USE_ACTION = 4\n\n  NORTH_DIR = 0\n  EAST_DIR = 1\n  SOUTH_DIR = 2\n  WEST_DIR = 3\n\n  # Helper function: Calculates direction agent needs to face to look at an item\n  def _get_target_facing_direction(agent_x, agent_y, item_x, item_y):\n    dx = item_x - agent_x\n    dy = item_y - agent_y\n\n    if dx == 0 and dy == 0:\n      return None # Agent is on top of the item, or item is at agent's exact spot - should not happen for collection\n\n    # Determine primary axis movement (horizontal or vertical) for facing\n    # Prioritize horizontal if dx magnitude is greater or equal, otherwise vertical\n    if abs(dx) >= abs(dy):\n      return EAST_DIR if dx > 0 else WEST_DIR\n    else: # abs(dy) > abs(dx)\n      return SOUTH_DIR if dy > 0 else NORTH_DIR\n\n  # Helper function: Returns actions to turn from current_dir to target_dir.\n  def _get_turn_actions(current_dir, target_dir):\n    actions = []\n    if current_dir == target_dir:\n      return []\n\n    clockwise_turns = (target_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n    counter_clockwise_turns = (current_dir - target_dir + 4) % 4\n\n    if clockwise_turns <= counter_clockwise_turns:\n      for _ in range(clockwise_turns):\n        actions.append(RIGHT_ACTION) # Turn right\n    else:\n      for _ in range(counter_clockwise_turns):\n        actions.append(LEFT_ACTION) # Turn left\n    return actions\n\n  primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  agent_grid = current_state.grid\n  agent_pos_x, agent_pos_y = current_state.pos\n  agent_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction\n\n  grid_height, grid_width, _ = agent_grid.shape\n\n  # Define a unified set of indices for entities that cannot be traversed by the agent.\n  # This includes non-grabbable items, workshop locations, and the primitive itself\n  # (as the agent cannot move *onto* the item it intends to collect).\n  impassable_indices = set()\n  impassable_indices.update(env.world.non_grabbable_indices)\n  impassable_indices.update(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  impassable_indices.add(primitive_id) \n\n  # Helper function to check if a grid cell is traversable.\n  def is_traversable(x, y):\n    # Check bounds first\n    if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n      return False \n    \n    # Check if the cell is occupied by any impassable item\n    for idx in impassable_indices:\n        if agent_grid[y, x, idx] == 1:\n            return False \n    return True # Cell is traversable\n\n  # Find all actual locations of the primitive on the grid.\n  y_coords, x_coords = np.where(agent_grid[:, :, primitive_id] == 1)\n\n  if len(x_coords) == 0:\n    return [] # Primitive not found on the grid\n\n  # Step 1: Identify all potential collection points.\n  # These are traversable cells from which the agent can be adjacent to *any* instance of the primitive.\n  primitive_locations = set()\n  for i in range(len(x_coords)):\n    primitive_locations.add((x_coords[i], y_coords[i]))\n  \n  potential_collection_points = set()\n  # Define deltas for checking cardinal adjacency (N, S, E, W)\n  ADJACENCY_DELTAS = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)] \n\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    for dx, dy in ADJACENCY_DELTAS:\n      adj_x, adj_y = px + dx, py + dy\n      if is_traversable(adj_x, adj_y): # Use the refined traversability check\n        potential_collection_points.add((adj_x, adj_y))\n  \n  if not potential_collection_points:\n      return [] # No valid collection points exist (e.g., item might be completely surrounded by obstacles)\n\n  # Step 2: BFS Pathfinding to *any* of the potential_collection_points.\n  # The BFS aims to find the shortest sequence of movement actions.\n  queue = [(agent_pos_x, agent_pos_y, [])] # (x, y, path_actions)\n  visited = set([(agent_pos_x, agent_pos_y)])\n  \n  path_to_adj_pos = []\n  chosen_adj_pos = None # The specific adjacent position the agent will move to\n  target_item_pos_for_facing = None # The specific primitive instance to face (for the USE action)\n\n  # Define movement deltas for BFS. These actions move the agent cardinally but\n  # do NOT change the agent's facing direction.\n  ACTION_MOVES = {\n      UP_ACTION: (0, -1),\n      DOWN_ACTION: (0, 1),\n      LEFT_ACTION: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT_ACTION: (1, 0),\n  }\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_x, curr_y, current_path = queue.pop(0)\n\n    # If the current position is one of the target collection points, we've found a path.\n    if (curr_x, curr_y) in potential_collection_points:\n      path_to_adj_pos = current_path\n      chosen_adj_pos = (curr_x, curr_y)\n      \n      # Now, identify *which* primitive instance this chosen_adj_pos is adjacent to.\n      # Any adjacent primitive instance will do for determining facing direction.\n      for dx, dy in ADJACENCY_DELTAS:\n          item_x, item_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n          if 0 <= item_x < grid_width and 0 <= item_y < grid_height and\\\n             agent_grid[item_y, item_x, primitive_id] == 1:\n              target_item_pos_for_facing = (item_x, item_y)\n              break # Found an adjacent primitive instance\n      break # Path found to a valid collection point, exit BFS\n\n    # Explore possible moves from the current position\n    for action, (dx, dy) in ACTION_MOVES.items():\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n\n      # If the next cell is traversable and hasn't been visited yet, add it to the queue.\n      if is_traversable(next_x, next_y) and (next_x, next_y) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n        queue.append((next_x, next_y, current_path + [action]))\n\n  # If no path was found to any collection point after exhausting the queue\n  if chosen_adj_pos is None:\n    return []\n\n  final_actions = list(path_to_adj_pos)\n\n  # After moving to the chosen_adj_pos, the agent's facing direction is still `agent_dir`\n  # (its initial direction, as movement actions don't change facing).\n  # We need to add turning actions to face the primitive from the new position.\n  if target_item_pos_for_facing is not None:\n    target_face_dir = _get_target_facing_direction(chosen_adj_pos[0], chosen_adj_pos[1], \n                                                   target_item_pos_for_facing[0], target_item_pos_for_facing[1])\n    if target_face_dir is not None:\n      # Turn from the agent's initial direction to the required target direction\n      final_actions.extend(_get_turn_actions(agent_dir, target_face_dir))\n  \n  # Finally, perform the USE action to collect the primitive\n  final_actions.append(USE_ACTION)\n\n  return final_actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
