{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T22:57:57.129356", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections # Required for deque\n\n  # Define action constants based on CraftLab.action_specs()\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # Access the initial CraftState from the CraftLab environment.\n  # This provides the starting point for our pathfinding.\n  initial_state = env._current_state\n\n  # If the primitive is already in the agent's inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if initial_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Initialize a queue for Breadth-First Search (BFS).\n  # Each item in the queue is a tuple: (current_CraftState, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state)\n  q = collections.deque([(initial_state, [])])\n\n  # Initialize a set to keep track of visited states to avoid cycles and redundant exploration.\n  # A state is defined by the agent's (position, direction).\n  visited = set([(initial_state.pos, initial_state.dir)])\n\n  # Set a maximum search depth to prevent excessively long computations or infinite loops\n  # in case of complex or unsolvable scenarios.\n  MAX_SEARCH_DEPTH = 50 \n\n  while q:\n    current_state, actions_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current state satisfies the goal condition:\n    # Is the primitive located in a cell adjacent to the agent?\n    if current_state.next_to(primitive):\n      # If so, append the USE action to the sequence and return the complete path.\n      # We assume that if a primitive is next to the agent, the USE action will successfully collect it.\n      return actions_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n    \n    # If the current path has exceeded the maximum allowed search depth,\n    # prune this branch to avoid exploring overly long or unpromising paths.\n    if len(actions_so_far) >= MAX_SEARCH_DEPTH:\n      continue\n\n    # Explore all possible movement actions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) from the current state.\n    for action in [ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_UP, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT]:\n      # Simulate the effect of taking this action.\n      # CraftState.step returns a tuple: (reward, new_state). We only care about the new_state.\n      _reward, next_state = current_state.step(action)\n\n      # Create a unique key for the next state to check if it has been visited before.\n      next_state_key = (next_state.pos, next_state.dir)\n      \n      # If this state has not been visited, add it to the visited set and the queue for further exploration.\n      if next_state_key not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_state_key)\n        q.append((next_state, actions_so_far + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive was found, return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
